ido a una holgura aumentada del orificio.INFECCI√ìN DE LA HERIDA:La infecci√≥n de la herida es un riesgo asociado a la realizaci√≥n de una intervenci√≥n quir√∫rgica, especialmente en pacientes con condiciones de salud comprometidas.DIABETES MELLITUS TIPO:La diabetes mellitus tipo es una condici√≥n m√©dica que puede aumentar el riesgo de infecci√≥n en pacientes que se someten a la gastrostom√≠a endosc√≥pica percut√°nea.GEP:GEP refers to Gastrostomy Enteral Feeding, a medical procedure involving the placement of a tube for nutritional support in patients who cannot eat by mouth.BRONCOASPIRATION:Broncoaspiration is a medical event where food or liquid enters the lungs, often leading to pneumonia and respiratory complications in patients receiving enteral nutrition.GRANULOMA:Granuloma formation is a complication that can occur in patients with GEP, characterized by an abnormal tissue response to irritation or infection.ASPIRATION PNEUMONIA:DIARREA INFECCIOSA:La diarrea infecciosa es una complicaci√≥n que puede ocurrir en pacientes que reciben nutrici√≥n enteral, caracterizada por la presencia de heces l√≠quidas causadas por infecciones.ESTOMA:El estoma es una abertura creada quir√∫rgicamente que permite la salida de desechos del cuerpo, y puede estar sujeto a infecciones en pacientes con nutrici√≥n enteral.HIPOFOFATEMIA:Hipofosfatemia is a condition of low phosphate levels that can occur in patients with inadequate nutritional intake or refeeding syndrome.AGITACI√ìN PSICOMOTRIZ:A condition characterized by restlessness and inability to remain still, which can occur in patients with decreased consciousness due to medical interventionsTRASTORNO DEPRESIVO:SCCM:Society of Critical Care Medicine, which provides guidelines for nutrition support therapy in critically ill patientsPARROTT F:Parrott F is one of the authors involved in the multicentre trial comparing nutritional support methods in critically ill patients.HARRISON DA:Harrison DA is one of the authors involved in the multicentre trial comparing nutritional support methods in critically ill patients.SADIQUE MZ:Sadique MZ is one of the authors involved in the multicentre trial comparing nutritional support methods in critically ill patients.GRIEVE RD:Grieve RD is one of the authors involved in the multicentre trial comparing nutritional support methods in critically ill patients.CANTER RR:Canter RR is one of the authors involved in the multicentre trial comparing nutritional support methods in critically ill patients.BROWN B:Brown B is one of the authors discussing enteral nutrition formula selection and its implications for practice.ROEHL K:Roehl K is one of the authors discussing enteral nutrition formula selection and its implications for practice.BETZ M:Betz M is one of the authors discussing enteral nutrition formula selection and its implications for practice.VANDEWOUDE MF:Vandewoude MF is one of the authors discussing fibre-supplemented tube feeding in hospitalized elderly patients.PARIDAENS KM:Paridaens KM is one of the authors discussing fibre-supplemented tube feeding in hospitalized elderly patients.SUY RA:Suy RA is one of the authors discussing fibre-supplemented tube feeding in hospitalized elderly patients.BOONE MA:Boone MA is one of the authors discussing fibre-supplemented tube feeding in hospitalized elderly patients.STROBBE H:Strobbe H is one of the authors discussing fibre-supplemented tube feeding in hospitalized elderly patients.ENGFER MB:Engfer MB is one of the authors involved in the systematic review and meta-analysis of fibre-containing enteral formulae.GREEN CJ:Green CJ is one of the authors involved in the systematic review and meta-analysis of fibre-containing enteral formulae.SILK DB:Silk DB is one of the authors involved in the systematic review and meta-analysis of fibre-containing enteral formulae.VANEK VW:Vanek VW is an author recognized for significant contributions to the field of parenteral nutrition. They have authored a position paper that explores the clinical role of alternative intravenous fat emulsions, highlighting their importance in nutritional therapy. Additionally, Vanek VW is one of the authors involved in developing guidelines for nutrition support therapy specifically tailored for critically ill patients, further emphasizing their expertise and influence in this area of healthcare.WARREN MM:Warren MM is one of the authors discussing guidelines for nutrition support therapy in critically ill patients.JOHNSON DR:Johnson DR is one of the authors discussing guidelines for nutrition support therapy in critically ill patients.TIENGOU LE:Tiengou LE is one of the authors discussing the choice between semi-elemental and polymeric formula for enteral nutrition in acute pancreatitis.GLORO R:Gloro R is one of the authors discussing the choice between semi-elemental and polymeric formula for enteral nutrition in acute pancreatitis.POUZOULET J:Pouzoulet J is one of the authors discussing the choice between semi-elemental and polymeric formula for enteral nutrition in acute pancreatitis.BOUHER K:Bouhier K is one of the authors discussing the choice between semi-elemental and polymeric formula for enteral nutrition in acute pancreatitis.READ MH:Read MH is one of the authors discussing the choice between semi-elemental and polymeric formula for enteral nutrition in acute pancreatitis.ARNAUD-BATTANDIER F:Arnaud-Battandier F is one of the authors discussing the choice between semi-elemental and polymeric formula for enteral nutrition in acute pancreatitis.TAYLOR AL:Taylor AL is one of the authors discussing probiotic supplementation in high-risk children.DUNSTAN JA:Dunstan JA is one of the authors discussing probiotic supplementation in high-risk children.PRESCOTT SL:Prescott SL is one of the authors discussing probiotic supplementation in high-risk children.DEJONG C:Dejong C is one of the authors discussing ESPEN guidelines on enteral nutrition in gastroenterology.HAMMARQVIST F:Hammarqvist F is one of the authors discussing ESPEN guidelines on enteral nutrition in gastroenterology.HEBUTERNE X:Hebuterne X is a researcher recognized for significant contributions to the field of home enteral nutrition and its practices across Europe. Additionally, Hebuterne X is one of the authors involved in discussing the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism (ESPEN) guidelines pertaining to enteral nutrition in gastroenterology.MCMANON MM:McMahon MM is one of the authors discussing treatment outcomes of early enteral versus early parenteral nutrition.CLINICAL GUIDELINES TASK FORCE:The Clinical Guidelines Task Force is a specialized group within the American Society for Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (ASPEN) dedicated to the development of clinical guidelines for nutrition support therapy. This task force focuses on creating evidence-based guidelines aimed at optimizing nutrition support for patients, ensuring that healthcare providers have access to the best practices in the field.HARVEY SE:SOCIETY OF CRITICAL CARE MEDICINE:The Society of Critical Care Medicine (SCCM) is a professional organization dedicated to enhancing the care of critically ill patients. It focuses on various aspects of critical care, including the development of guidelines for nutrition support therapy. The organization aims to improve patient outcomes through research, education, and the establishment of best practices in critical care medicine.MUELLER CM:Mueller CM is an editor and contributor to various works on nutrition support and critical care.PETER JV:Peter JV is a researcher who has contributed to studies on treatment outcomes in hospitalized patients.WANG K:Wang K is a researcher involved in studies regarding enteral tube feeding intolerance.HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO R√çO HORTEGA:Hospital Universitario R√≠o Hortega is a medical facility situated in Valladolid, Spain. It specializes in endocrinology and nutrition, providing comprehensive healthcare services in these fields.INSTITUTO DE ENDOCRINOLOG√çA Y NUTRICI√ìN:VALLADOLID:Valladolid is a city in Spain known for its significant contributions to the fields of endocrinology and nutrition. It is home to the Centro de Investigaci√≥n de Endocrinolog√≠a y Nutrici√≥n, a research center dedicated to advancing knowledge in these areas. Additionally, the city houses the Hospital Cl√≠nico Universitario, which plays a crucial role in clinical care and research. Valladolid has also been referenced in publications related to clinical nutrition and metabolism, highlighting its importance in the academic and medical communities.ALIMENTACI√ìN POR V√çA ENTERAL:The method of providing nutrition directly into the gastrointestinal tract through a tube, which has been referenced since 1589.SONDAS:Sondas are medical devices specifically designed for enteral feeding, which includes various types of tubes such as nasogastric, nasoduodenal, and nasojejunal tubes. They are utilized to provide nutrition to patients who are unable to consume food orally. Additionally, Sondas can be used for feeding patients through gastrostomy or jejunostomy, offering a range of types and sizes to accommodate different patient needs. Overall, Sondas play a crucial role in the administration of enteral nutrition when oral intake is not feasible.SONDA NASOENT√âRICA:A nasoenteric tube is a type of feeding tube that is inserted through the nose and extends into the small intestine, used for patients requiring long-term nutritional support.ALGORITMO PARA LA ELECCI√ìN DE ACCESO EN NUTRICI√ìN ENTERAL:An algorithm designed to guide the choice of access for enteral nutrition, considering patient conditions and risks.PEREIRA JL:Pereira JL is a researcher who plays a significant role in the recommendations for managing hyperglycemia in patients receiving artificial nutrition. Additionally, Pereira JL is recognized as an author referenced in the context of enteral nutrition guidelines and practices, contributing valuable insights to the field.LAPAROTOM√çA:Laparotom√≠a is a surgical procedure that involves making an incision into the abdominal cavity. This procedure is often utilized to access internal organs for various medical interventions. It may impact a patient's ability to tolerate enteral nutrition. The term "laparotom√≠a" is the Spanish equivalent of "laparotomy," and both descriptions highlight its role in surgical practices, particularly in relation to the abdominal wall.TRAUMATISMO CRANEOENCEF√ÅLICO:Traumatismo craneoencef√°lico, or cranioencephalic trauma, refers to injuries affecting both the brain and skull. This type of traumatic brain injury can complicate enteral feeding processes and may lead to serious complications, necessitating immediate medical attention. Additionally, it can result in conditions such as SIADH (Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion), and the duration of treatment for such injuries can vary significantly. Overall, Traumatismo craneoencef√°lico represents a critical medical condition that requires prompt and effective management.MIXEDEMA:Myxedema is a severe form of hypothyroidism that can affect a patient's metabolism and nutritional requirements.FIADOR:El fiador es un dispositivo que facilita la colocaci√≥n de la sonda, proporcionando rigidez y evitando la perforaci√≥n durante el procedimiento.HIGIENE BUCAL:La higiene bucal es un procedimiento que se debe mantener adecuadamente en los d√≠as sucesivos tras la colocaci√≥n de la sonda para evitar complicaciones.RADIOL√ìGICA:La comprobaci√≥n radiol√≥gica es el m√©todo m√°s seguro para verificar la posici√≥n correcta de la sonda tras su colocaci√≥n.OBSTRUCCI√ìN:La obstrucci√≥n es una complicaci√≥n que puede ocurrir en el uso de sondas, afectando hasta el 9% de los casos.COMPROBACI√ìN:La comprobaci√≥n de la posici√≥n de la sonda es un paso crucial para asegurar su correcta colocaci√≥n y funcionamiento.PACIENTE CON RIESGO DE BRONCOASPIRACI√ìN:El paciente con riesgo de broncoaspiraci√≥n es aquel que no debe recibir una Sonda Nasog√°strica debido a complicaciones potenciales.√çLEO EN EL COLON:El √≠leo en el colon es una condici√≥n que puede durar de 3 a 5 d√≠as, afectando el tr√°nsito intestinal.NEUMON√çA ASPIRATIVA:NEUMON√çA ASPIRATIVA is a serious complication that can arise from the use of enteral feeding tubes. This condition occurs when food or liquid inadvertently enters the lungs, leading to potential respiratory issues. In Spanish, it is described as a grave complication that can occur due to the entry of digestive contents into the respiratory tract.COMPROBACI√ìN RADIOLOGICA:La comprobaci√≥n radiol√≥gica es un procedimiento utilizado para confirmar la correcta colocaci√≥n de la sonda nasog√°strica o nasoenteral.PONSKEY:PONSKEY is recognized as one of the pioneers of the endoscopic gastrostomy technique, significantly contributing to advancements in minimally invasive feeding procedures.GAUDEREZ:GAUDEREZ is a medical professional recognized for co-developing the endoscopic gastrostomy technique, which significantly improved patient care in nutritional support. In 1979, Gauderez was among the first physicians to practice endoscopic gastrostomy, contributing to the establishment of this technique as the preferred method for enteral nutrition.ALTERACI√ìN DEL NIVEL DE CONSCIENCIA:A medical condition where a patient experiences changes in awareness or responsiveness, which can be critical in assessing overall health.HERNIAS HIATAL:A condition where part of the stomach pushes through the diaphragm into the chest cavity, often leading to complications in digestion.OBSTRUCCI√ìN G√ÅSTRICA:A blockage in the stomach that prevents food from passing into the small intestine, requiring medical intervention.COMPLICACIONES INFECCIOSAS LOCALES:Local infectious complications that can arise from medical procedures, such as otitis and sinusitis, affecting patient recovery.COMPLICACIONES MEC√ÅNICAS:Mechanical complications that can occur from the use of medical devices, such as injuries from pressure sores or local infections.CUIDADOS DE LA SONDA:The practices involved in maintaining and caring for feeding tubes to prevent complications and ensure patient safety.ACCESO INVASIVO AL TUBO DIGESTIVO:A medical procedure that involves creating an opening in the digestive tract for feeding or other interventions.PROCESOS FUNCIONALES:Functional disorders of the digestive system that may necessitate surgical interventions like enterostomies.INFECCIONES ABDOMINALES ACTIVAS:Active abdominal infections that can pose risks during surgical procedures, necessitating careful evaluation.ENFERMEDADES NEUROL√ìGICAS DEGENERATIVAS:Degenerative neurological diseases that can affect swallowing and digestion, leading to the need for nutritional support.T√âCNICAS ENDOSC√ìPICAS:Minimally invasive procedures performed using an endoscope, often preferred for their lower risk and quicker recovery times.)<|COMPLETE|>T√âCNICA DE PONSKY-GAUDERER:La t√©cnica de Ponsky-Gauderer es un m√©todo espec√≠fico para realizar una gastrostom√≠a endosc√≥pica, que implica el uso de un endoscopio y anestesia t√≥pica para facilitar la inserci√≥n de la sonda.T√âCNICA DE SACKS-VINE:La t√©cnica de Sacks-Vine es un m√©todo de colocaci√≥n de sonda de gastrostom√≠a que se realiza bajo visi√≥n endosc√≥pica, utilizando una aguja introductora para guiar el cat√©ter al est√≥mago.T√âCNICA DE RUSSELL:La t√©cnica de Russell es un procedimiento percut√°neo para la colocaci√≥n de una sonda de gastrostom√≠a, que utiliza un bal√≥n tipo Foley y control endosc√≥pico para asegurar la correcta colocaci√≥n de la sonda.YEYUNOSTOM√çA ENDOSC√ìPICA:La yeyunostom√≠a endosc√≥pica es un procedimiento que permite la inserci√≥n de una sonda en el yeyuno, indicado para pacientes con riesgo de aspiraci√≥n, manteniendo la motilidad y funci√≥n absortiva del intestino.ANESTESIA LOCAL:Anestesia local is a type of anesthesia utilized in various medical procedures, including faringostom√≠a and gastrostom√≠a endosc√≥pica. Its primary purpose is to minimize pain in the specific area being treated, allowing for the procedure to be performed with reduced risk of complications compared to general anesthesia. This localized approach enhances patient safety and comfort during interventions.FARINGOSTOM√çA:Faringostom√≠a is a surgical procedure for placing a feeding tube through the piriform sinus into the neck, indicated for trauma or malformations.MALFORMACIONES:Malformaciones are congenital anomalies that may require surgical procedures such as faringostom√≠a for feeding.OSTOM√çAS QUIR√öRGICAS:YEYUNOSTOM√çA QUIR√öRGICA:Yeyunostom√≠a quir√∫rgica is a surgical procedure performed as a complement to gastrointestinal surgery to avoid risks associated with parenteral nutrition.T√âCNICA DE STAMM:T√©cnica de Stamm is a simple method for gastrostomy, suitable for high surgical risk cases or temporary gastrostomy.T√âCNICA DE WITZEL:T√©cnica de Witzel involves creating a seromuscular tunnel around the catheter to reduce leakage risk during yeyunostom√≠a.T√âCNICA DE JANEWAY:T√©cnica de Janeway is a method for permanent gastrostomy using a Foley catheter within a gastric tunnel.OSTOM√çAS RADIOLOGICAS:Ostom√≠as radiol√≥gicas refer to procedures like gastrostom√≠a radiol√≥gica percut√°nea, which do not require anesthesia or endoscopy.ANESTESIA GENERAL:ANESTESIA GENERAL is a medical procedure utilized to induce unconsciousness in patients during surgical operations, including procedures such as the placement of feeding tubes. While it is essential for facilitating various surgeries, ANESTESIA GENERAL also carries inherent risks associated with surgical interventions.COMPLICACIONES DE LAS SONDAS DE YEYUNOSTOM√çA:Complicaciones de las sondas de yeyunostom√≠a refer to potential issues that can arise from the use of feeding tubes in the jejunum, including obstruction and infection.CAT√âTER FINO:Cat√©ter fino is a thin tube used in medical procedures, particularly in yeyunostom√≠a, to facilitate feeding directly into the jejunum.TUBO DE ALIMENTACI√ìN:HERNIA HIATAL:A condition where part of the stomach pushes through the diaphragm into the chest cavity, which can complicate certain medical procedures.ATROPINA:A medication used to reduce saliva and secretions during medical procedures, often administered subcutaneously.DILATADORES:Devices used to gradually widen an opening, often used in medical procedures to facilitate the insertion of catheters.CAT√âTER DE GASTROSTOM√çA:A tube inserted into the stomach for the purpose of providing nutritional support directly to patients.T√âCNICA ENDOSC√ìPICA:A minimally invasive procedure that uses an endoscope to access the digestive tract for various medical interventions.SONDA POSTPIL√ìRICA:A type of feeding tube placed beyond the pylorus in the small intestine, used in patients at risk of aspiration.METHENY NA:Metheny NA is a researcher who has contributed to studies on feeding tube aspirates and their implications in medical practice.STEWART BJ:Stewart BJ is a researcher involved in studies related to nutrition and feeding tube placement.SMITH L:Smith L is a researcher who has co-authored studies on feeding tube aspirates.YAN H:Yan H is a researcher who has contributed to studies on feeding tube aspirates.DIEBOLD M:Diebold M is a researcher involved in studies on feeding tube aspirates.CLOUSE RE:Clouse RE is a researcher who has co-authored studies on feeding tube aspirates.HENDRY PJ:Hendry PJ is a researcher who has studied complications related to nasogastric feeding tubes.AKYUREKLI Y:Akyurekli Y is a researcher involved in studies on nasogastric feeding tubes.MCINTYRE R:Mcintyre R is a researcher who has contributed to studies on nasogastric feeding tubes.QUARRINGTON A:Quarrington A is a researcher involved in studies on nasogastric feeding tubes.KEON WJ:Keon WJ is a researcher who has studied bronchopleural complications of nasogastric feeding tubes.CISNEROS C:Cisneros C is a researcher who has studied the penetration of nasogastric tubes in