ed pulmonary aspiration in hospitalized adults.IBA√ëEZ J:Iba√±ez J is a researcher involved in studies on gastroesophageal reflux in intubated patients.PE√ëAFIEL A:Pe√±afiel A is a researcher who has contributed to studies on gastroesophageal reflux.RAURICH JM:Raurich JM is a researcher involved in studies on gastroesophageal reflux.MARSE P:Marse P is a researcher who has studied the effects of patient positioning on gastroesophageal reflux.JORD√Å R:Jord√° R is a researcher involved in studies on gastroesophageal reflux.MATA F:Mata F is a researcher who has contributed to studies on gastroesophageal reflux.CHERYL ANN MONTURO:Cheryl Ann Monturo is a researcher who has studied enteral access device selection.GUADERER MWL:Guaderer MWL is a researcher involved in studies on gastrostomy techniques.PONSKY JL:Ponsky JL is a researcher who has contributed to studies on gastrostomy techniques.IZANT RJ:Izant RJ is a researcher involved in studies on gastrostomy techniques.STIEGMANN G:Stiegmann G is a researcher who has studied operative versus endoscopic gastrostomy.COFF J:Coff J is a researcher involved in studies on gastrostomy techniques.VAN WAY C:Van Way C is a researcher who has contributed to studies on gastrostomy techniques.PERINO LL:Perino LL is a researcher involved in studies on gastrostomy techniques.PEARLMAN N:Pearlman N is a researcher who has studied gastrostomy techniques.NORTON L:Norton L is a researcher involved in studies on gastrostomy techniques.RUSSELL TR:Russell TR is a researcher who has studied percutaneous gastrostomy techniques.BROTMAN M:Brotman M is a researcher involved in studies on percutaneous gastrostomy.NORRIS P:Norris P is a researcher who has contributed to studies on percutaneous gastrostomy.BEATEN CGMY:Beaten CGMY is a researcher involved in studies on percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy.VISMANS FJFE:Vismans FJFE is a researcher who has studied percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy.VON MEYENFELDT MF:Von Meyenfeldt MF is a researcher involved in studies on percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy.DE GREGORIO MA<|("ENTITY":PERSONCELAYA S:Celaya S is a researcher who has contributed to studies on percutaneous gastrostomy techniques.CIVEIRA E:Civeira E is a researcher involved in studies on percutaneous gastrostomy.ALFONSO R:Alfonso R is a researcher who has studied percutaneous gastrostomy techniques.FERN√ÅNDEZ J:Fern√°ndez J is a researcher involved in studies on percutaneous gastrostomy.ARI√ëO I:Ari√±o I is a researcher who has contributed to studies on percutaneous gastrostomy.CAVE DR:Cave DR is a researcher who has studied complications following percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy.ROBINSON WR:Robinson WR is a researcher involved in studies on complications of percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy.BROTSCHI EA:Brotschi EA is a researcher who has studied complications following percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy.DITESHEIM JA:Ditesheim JA is a researcher involved in studies on complications of percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy.RICHARDS W:Richards W is a researcher who has studied complications following percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy.SHARPK:Sharp K is a researcher involved in studies on complications of percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy.FATAL AND DISASTROUS COMPLICATIONS:A study focusing on the fatal and disastrous complications following percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy.PERCUTANEOUS ENDOSCOPIC GASTROSTOMY:A minimally invasive technique for placing a feeding tube into the stomach.NASOGASTRIC FEEDING TUBES:A medical device used for delivering nutrition directly to the stomach through the nose.)<|COMPLETE|>INSTITUTO DE INVESTIGACI√ìN DE ENDOCRINOLOG√çA Y NUTRICI√ìN:The Instituto de Investigaci√≥n de Endocrinolog√≠a y Nutrici√≥n is a research institute focused on endocrinology and nutrition.FACULTAD DE MEDICINA, UNIVERSIDAD DE VALLADOLID:The Facultad de Medicina at the Universidad de Valladolid is an educational institution that trains medical professionals.NUTRICI√ìN PARENTERAL SUPLEMENTARIA:NUTRICI√ìN PARENTERAL SUPLEMENTARIA (NPS) es un enfoque terap√©utico indicado para pacientes postquir√∫rgicos que necesitan un aporte nutricional adicional cuando la alimentaci√≥n enteral resulta insuficiente. Este tipo de nutrici√≥n complementa la alimentaci√≥n enteral en aquellos pacientes que no pueden satisfacer completamente sus necesidades nutricionales a trav√©s de esta v√≠a.NUTRICI√ìN PARENTERAL HOSPITALARIA:NUTRICI√ìN PARENTERAL HOSPITALARIA refers to the administration of nutrients intravenously in a hospital setting. This method, known as hospital parenteral nutrition (NPH), is utilized to provide essential nutrition to patients who are unable to receive adequate nourishment through oral or enteral means. NPH is often evaluated in cost-effectiveness studies, highlighting its importance in clinical nutrition management during hospitalization.ENTERITIS R√ÅDICA:La enteritis r√°dica es una inflamaci√≥n del intestino delgado que puede resultar de la radioterapia y puede llevar a la malabsorci√≥n, requiriendo nutrici√≥n parenteral en algunos casos.ENTEROCOLITIS NECROTIZANTE:La enterocolitis necrotizante es una enfermedad grave que afecta principalmente a reci√©n nacidos y puede causar da√±o intestinal severo, a menudo requiriendo nutrici√≥n parenteral.MALFORMACIONES CONG√âNITAS:Las malformaciones cong√©nitas son defectos presentes al nacer que pueden afectar la estructura y funci√≥n del intestino, a veces requiriendo nutrici√≥n parenteral para el manejo nutricional.S√çNDROMES ADHERENCIALES:Los s√≠ndromes adherenciales son condiciones en las que el tejido cicatricial causa adherencias en el intestino, lo que puede llevar a obstrucci√≥n y la necesidad de nutrici√≥n parenteral.ENFERMEDADES POR INCLUSI√ìN DE LAS MICROVELLOSIDADES:Estas enfermedades afectan la superficie intestinal y pueden causar malabsorci√≥n, llevando a la necesidad de nutrici√≥n parenteral en algunos pacientes.ENTERITIS AUTOINMUNES:Las enteritis autoinmunes son condiciones en las que el sistema inmunol√≥gico ataca el intestino, lo que puede resultar en malabsorci√≥n y requerir nutrici√≥n parenteral.)<|COMPLETE|>SERVICIOS DE FARMACIA HOSPITALARIA:Los Servicios de Farmacia Hospitalaria son unidades especializadas que tienen la responsabilidad de elaborar nutrici√≥n parenteral individualizada. Estas unidades se enfocan en adaptar las dietas a las necesidades espec√≠ficas de cada paciente, especialmente en el contexto de pacientes cr√≠ticos. Su labor es fundamental para garantizar que cada paciente reciba la nutrici√≥n adecuada seg√∫n sus requerimientos m√©dicos particulares.NUTRICI√ìN PARENTERAL INDIVIDUALIZADA:ESTR√âS METAB√ìLICO SEVERO:El estr√©s metab√≥lico severo es una condici√≥n que puede contraindicar la administraci√≥n de nutrici√≥n parenteral, ya que los pacientes en esta situaci√≥n tienen requerimientos nutricionales especiales.FORMULACI√ìN 2 EN 1:La formulaci√≥n 2 en 1 es una mezcla de glucosa y amino√°cidos administrada con emulsi√≥n lip√≠dica de manera independiente, utilizada en nutrici√≥n parenteral para evitar interacciones de f√°rmacos.FORMULACI√ìN 3 EN 1:La formulaci√≥n 3 en 1 combina amino√°cidos, glucosa y l√≠pidos en una sola bolsa, reduciendo el riesgo de contaminaci√≥n y la manipulaci√≥n durante la administraci√≥n.AA RAMIFICADOS:Los amino√°cidos ramificados son un tipo de amino√°cidos que se utilizan en soluciones de nutrici√≥n parenteral para pacientes con condiciones cr√≠ticas, como encefalopat√≠a hep√°tica.ENFERMEDAD DE BASE:La enfermedad de base se refiere a la condici√≥n m√©dica subyacente que afecta las necesidades nutricionales de un paciente y su tratamiento.D-GLUCOSA:D-Glucose is a carbohydrate that serves as a primary energy source, playing a vital role in parenteral nutrition. It influences insulin secretion and contributes to nitrogen savings, making it essential for patients who require nutritional support. Additionally, D-Glucose is responsible for a significant portion of the osmolarity of parenteral nutrition solutions, further underscoring its importance in providing energy to patients.GRANDES QUEMADOS:Grandes quemados refers to patients with severe burns who have increased nutritional needs due to metabolic stress.PACIENTES POSTQUIR√öRGICOS:TCL INTRALIPID:TCL Intralipid is a product derived from soybean oil, used in lipid emulsions for nutritional support, particularly in providing essential fatty acids and influencing inflammatory responses.CLINOLEIC:Clinoleic is a 20% lipid emulsion utilized in parenteral nutrition, specifically formulated to deliver essential fatty acids. It is composed of a blend of soybean oil and olive oil, introduced in the late 1990s. Clinoleic is notable for its high content of oleic acid and vitamin E, which contribute to its nutritional benefits. As a third-generation lipid emulsion, it is enriched with olive oil, recognized for its high antioxidant content and its resistance to lipid peroxidation, making it a valuable option in clinical settings for patients requiring parenteral nutrition.ALPHA-TOCOPHEROL:Alpha-tocopherol is a form of vitamin E present in Clinoleic, known for its antioxidant properties and health benefits.ACIDOS GRASOS W3:Omega-3 fatty acids (AGW3) are incorporated into fourth-generation emulsions like Lipoplus, associated with anti-inflammatory effects.ACIDOS GRASOS W6:Omega-6 fatty acids (AGW6) are essential fatty acids that are present in high amounts in traditional lipid emulsions, influencing inflammatory responses.HIDRATACION:Hydration is a critical aspect of patient care, involving the management of fluid intake and losses to maintain health.BALANCE HIDRICO:Fluid balance refers to the careful management of fluid intake and output in patients to ensure proper hydration and physiological function.ACIDOS GRASOS:Fatty acids are key components of lipid emulsions, influencing their nutritional properties and effects on health.ACETATO:Acetato is a compound utilized in medical treatments, particularly recognized for its role as an additive in parenteral nutrition solutions. It serves multiple functions, including helping to maintain the body's acid-base balance and acting as a precursor to bicarbonate in cases of metabolic acidosis. Additionally, Acetato is a source of energy and is considered an essential electrolyte in the nutritional requirements for pediatric patients, particularly in parenteral nutrition. Overall, Acetato plays a crucial role in supporting the metabolic needs and pH balance of individuals receiving specialized nutritional care.G√ÅSTRICA:G√°strica refers to the gastric secretion in the stomach, which contains specific concentrations of electrolytes.I. DELGADO:I. delgado refers to the small intestine, which secretes fluids containing electrolytes during digestion.BILIS:Bilis is a digestive fluid produced by the liver that contains electrolytes and aids in digestion.PACIENTE ESTABLE:A stable patient who may require less intensive monitoring and nutritional support through parenteral nutrition.CR√ìMO:Chromium is also viewed as a contaminant in parenteral nutrition and should be limited in prolonged regimens.GLUCEMIA CAPILAR:Capillary blood glucose monitoring is essential for patients on parenteral nutrition to ensure stable glucose levels.PARAMETROS CL√çNICOS:Clinical parameters are essential metrics for assessing the health of patients on parenteral nutrition.PARAMETROS ANAL√çTICOS:Analytical parameters are critical for evaluating the biochemical status of patients receiving parenteral nutrition.SELECION DE OLIGOELEMENTOS:ASPARTATO AMINOTRANSFERASA:Aspartato Aminotransferasa is an enzyme that is commonly evaluated in blood tests to monitor liver function.GAMMA GLUTAMIL TRANSFERASA:Gamma Glutamil Transferasa is an enzyme that is used as a marker for liver disease and bile duct problems.PRUEBAS DE FUNCI√ìN HEP√ÅTICA:Pruebas de Funci√≥n Hep√°tica are a series of blood tests used to evaluate the health of the liver.ALANINA AMINOTRANSFERASA:ALTERACIONES HEPATOBILIARES:Alteraciones hepatobiliares refer to liver and biliary tract complications that can arise from prolonged parenteral nutrition.C√ÅTEDRA:C√°tedra refers to the complications associated with catheter use in patients receiving parenteral nutrition.COMPLICACIONES DE LA NUTRICI√ìN PARENTERAL:HIPERFOSFOREMIA:Hyperphosphatemia is a condition characterized by high phosphate levels in the blood, which can occur in patients with renal insufficiency.HEPATOBILIARY COMPLICATIONS:Complications that arise in the liver and bile ducts, often related to prolonged parenteral nutrition, including steatosis and cholestasis.INTESTINAL FAILURE:Intestinal failure is a medical condition characterized by the inability of the intestines to absorb sufficient nutrients and fluids, which often necessitates the use of parenteral nutrition. This condition predominantly affects pediatric patients, who may require home parenteral nutrition to manage their nutritional needs. Intestinal failure is considered a serious health issue and is frequently discussed in relation to liver disease and transplantation, highlighting its complexity and the critical care required for affected individuals.SOBRECRESCIMIENTO BACTERIANO:SOBRECRESCIMIENTO BACTERIANO is a condition characterized by an abnormal increase in bacteria in the intestines. This condition is particularly relevant for patients with intestinal failure, as it can significantly impact their liver health. In cases where patients are receiving parenteral nutrition, SOBRECRESCIMIENTO BACTERIANO may necessitate empirical treatment with metronidazole to manage the bacterial overgrowth effectively.TRASPLANTE AISLADO DE INTESTINO DELGADO:A surgical procedure to replace the small intestine, which can improve liver function in patients with hepatobiliary complications related to parenteral nutrition.HIPOMOTILIDAD INTESTINAL:La hipomotilidad intestinal es una condici√≥n que se refiere a la disminuci√≥n de la motilidad del intestino, lo que puede contribuir al fallo intestinal y a complicaciones como el sobrecrecimiento bacteriano.COLANGIO:El colangio es un t√©rmino que se refiere a los conductos biliares, que pueden verse afectados por el flujo biliar y la salud hep√°tica.ESTEATOSIS:La esteatosis es una acumulaci√≥n de grasa en el h√≠gado que puede ser causada por la nutrici√≥n parenteral y otros factores, afectando la funci√≥n hep√°tica.COLECISTOQUININA:La colecistoquinina es una hormona que estimula el flujo biliar y se ve afectada por la ingesta de nutrientes.SECRETINA:La secretina es una hormona que regula la producci√≥n de jugos digestivos y el flujo biliar, y su producci√≥n puede verse alterada en ausencia de est√≠mulo enteral.MOTILINA:La motilina es una hormona que regula la motilidad gastrointestinal y puede verse afectada por la nutrici√≥n parenteral.POLIPEPTIDO PANCREATICO:El polip√©ptido pancre√°tico es una hormona que regula la funci√≥n del p√°ncreas y puede influir en la digesti√≥n y el flujo biliar.OLIVEIRA FUSTER G.:Oliveira Fuster G. is an author recognized for his contributions to the field of clinical nutrition, particularly in the area of parenteral nutrition. He authored a practical guide that addresses the prescription and monitoring of parenteral nutrition, providing valuable insights for healthcare professionals. Additionally, he contributed to the "Manual de Nutrici√≥n Cl√≠nica y Diet√©tica," further emphasizing his expertise and focus on parenteral nutrition within clinical dietary practices.GONZ√ÅLEZ MOLERO I.:Gonz√°lez Molero I. is a notable author and co-author in the field of clinical nutrition, particularly focusing on parenteral nutrition. They contributed to the development of a practical guide on the prescription and monitoring of parenteral nutrition, showcasing their expertise in this area. Additionally, Gonz√°lez Molero I. collaborated on the "Manual de Nutrici√≥n Cl√≠nica y Diet√©tica," further emphasizing their specialization and commitment to advancing knowledge in clinical nutrition and dietary practices.TRASPLANTE DE INTESTINO DELGADO:Surgical procedure indicated for selected patients with severe intestinal failure.DENSITOMETR√çA MINERAL √ìSEA:Diagnostic procedure recommended for monitoring bone health in patients receiving parenteral nutrition.LIN LIM S.:Lin Lim S. is an author who studied the impact of malnutrition on hospitalization costs and outcomes.BRAGA M.:Braga M. is an author of the ESPEN guidelines on parenteral nutrition related to surgery.PITTIRUTI M.:Pittiruti M. is an author who contributed to the ESPEN guidelines on central venous catheters for parenteral nutrition.ANDERSON D.G.:Anderson D.G. is an author who researched peripheral parenteral nutrition.HOHEIM D.F.:Hoheim D.F. is an author who studied clinical experiences with three-in-one admixtures for parenteral nutrition.BAUER P.:Bauer P. is an author who researched the combination of parenteral and enteral nutrition in critically ill patients.DVIR D.:Dvir D. is an author who conducted an observational study on energy balance and complications in critically ill patients.VILLET S.:Villet S. is an author who studied the negative impact of hypocaloric feeding on clinical outcomes in ICU patients.KOVACEVICH D.S.:Kovacevich D.S. is an author who contributed to the standards for specialized nutrition support for home care patients.MIRTALLO J.:Mirtallo J. is an author involved in the task force for safe practices in parenteral nutrition.MIRTALLO J.M.:TASK FORCE FOR THE REVISION OF SAFE PRACTICES FOR PARENTERAL NUTRITION:The "TASK FORCE FOR THE REVISION OF SAFE PRACTICES FOR PARENTERAL NUTRITION" is a dedicated group that focuses on establishing and revising safe practices for parenteral nutrition. This task force plays a crucial role in contributing to guidelines and recommendations within the field of nutrition support therapy, ensuring that best practices are upheld to enhance patient safety and care.GERMAN SOCIETY FOR NUTRITIONAL MEDICINE:A professional organization that provides guidelines and recommendations for nutritional practices in Germany, particularly in clinical settings.EUROPEAN SOCIETY FOR PARENTERAL AND ENTERAL NUTRITION:A society that focuses on the promotion of safe and effective nutritional practices in Europe, including guidelines for parenteral nutrition.SURGICAL ICU PATIENTS:Patients in the surgical intensive care unit who may require specialized nutritional support due to their critical condition.ROLLINS CJ:An author who has discussed total nutrient admixtures and their stability issues in nursing practice.ERDMAN SH:An author involved in research on central line occlusion and its implications for parenteral nutrition.HARDY G:HARDY G is an author recognized for significant contributions to the formulation and stability of parenteral nutrition, particularly through the development of new lipid emulsions. In addition to this, Hardy G has also discussed essential principles for compounding parenteral nutrition admixtures, further enhancing the understanding and application of nutritional support in clinical settings.YARANDI SS:An author who has researched amino acid composition in parenteral nutrition.MUNDI MS:An author who has written about the management of parenteral nutrition in hospitalized adult patients.KREYMANN KG:An author who has contributed to the ESPEN guidelines on enteral nutrition in intensive care.MCGLAVE SA:MCGLAVE SA is an author known for providing guidelines for nutrition support therapy specifically aimed at critically ill patients. Their work focuses on establishing best practices and recommendations to enhance the nutritional care of individuals facing severe health challenges.SUN LC:An author who has conducted a randomized controlled study on branched-chain amino acid-enriched total parenteral nutrition.KUHN KS:An author who has researched the role of glutamine as an indispensable nutrient in oncology.GIANOTTI L:An author who has conducted a randomized multicenter trial on intravenous glutamine supplementation in major ab