 to research on complications of parenteral nutrition.SCHMIDT BF:Schmidt BF is an author involved in the study of complications of parenteral nutrition.MERMEL LA:Mermel LA is an author recognized for their contributions to the field of healthcare, specifically in the management of intravascular catheter-related infections. They have played a significant role in developing clinical practice guidelines aimed at addressing these types of infections, providing valuable insights and recommendations for healthcare professionals.FISIOPATOL√ìGIA:Fisiopatolog√≠a refers to the study of the functional changes that occur in the body as a result of a disease or condition, particularly in relation to nutrition and immune response.INFECCIONES RELACIONADAS CON CAT√âTERES:Infecciones relacionadas con cat√©teres refers to infections that occur due to the presence of intravascular catheters, which are addressed in clinical guidelines.NUTRIENTES INMUNOMODULADORES:Nutrientes inmunomoduladores are nutrients that can modify the immune response, particularly in the context of clinical nutrition.√ÅCIDOS OMEGA-3:Omega-3 fatty acids are immunonutrients with anti-inflammatory effects, reducing pro-inflammatory cytokines and acting at the nuclear level in NFkB.ACIDO ARAQUIDONICO:Arachidonic acid is a polyunsaturated fatty acid that plays a key role in inflammatory responses and is a precursor to various eicosanoids.GLUTATI√ìN:Glutati√≥n is a tripeptide that plays a critical role in cellular antioxidant defense and is synthesized from glutamine, cysteine, and glycine.CICATRIZACI√ìN DE HERIDAS:Cicatrizaci√≥n de heridas refers to the process of healing injuries, which arginine is known to enhance.INTESTINO:Intestino is the organ that primarily receives glutamine during stress, playing a vital role in nutrient absorption and immune function.NFKB/IKB:GOTTSCHLICH ET AL:Gottschlich et al. conducted a study involving 50 patients with burn injuries to evaluate the effects of an immunomodulatory diet.SAFFLE ET AL:Saffle et al. compared an immunomodulatory formula against a standard formula without arginine in a study involving burn patients.BROWN ET AL:Brown et al. conducted a study on critically ill patients to assess the impact of an immunomodulatory formula on infection rates.KUDSK ET AL:Kudsk et al. performed a study with 70 patients to evaluate the effectiveness of an immunomodulatory diet in reducing infections.BURN INJURIES:Burn injuries refer to the medical condition of patients who have suffered burns, which were the focus of several studies on immunonutrition.VEGENAT MED:Vegenat Med is a brand that produces glutamine supplements, specifically designed for nutritional support in clinical settings.GLUTAMINA NM:Glutamina NM is a brand that provides glutamine supplements, focusing on high-quality nutritional support.KABI:Kabi is a company that manufactures glutamine products for medical and nutritional use.MOORE ET AL.:Moore et al. refers to a group of researchers who conducted a multicenter study on immunonutrition and its effects on patient outcomes.MENDEZ:Mendez is a researcher who published findings on the effects of immunonutrition, noting negative outcomes in certain patient groups.WEIMANN ET AL.:Weimann et al. refers to a group of researchers who studied the incidence of pneumonia in patients receiving immunonutrition.RESOURCE SUPPORT:Resource Support is a nutritional product designed to provide essential nutrients for patients requiring dietary assistance.SUPORTAN DRINK:Suportan Drink is a nutritional beverage designed to provide essential nutrients for patients in clinical settings.ATEMPERO:Atempero is a nutritional product formulated to support patients' dietary needs, particularly in critical care.BOWER:Bower conducted a multicenter study involving 326 patients to evaluate the effects of immunonutrition in critical patients.RODRIGO CASANOVA:Rodrigo Casanova is a researcher who found lower incidence of pneumonia in patients receiving immunomodulatory formulas.GALBAN:Galban conducted research that detected lower mortality rates with immunomodulatory formulas.GRUPO ITALIANO COLABORATIVO:A collaborative Italian group that compared parenteral nutrition with immunomodulatory formulas in critically ill patients.F√ìRMULA INMUNOMODULADORA:F√ìRMULA INMUNOMODULADORA is a type of nutritional formula utilized in studies to assess its effects on critically ill patients.SEPSIS NO SEVERA:A less severe condition that was also included in the study comparing nutritional methods.DALY:Daly is a researcher who conducted a study on the effects of immunomodulatory formulas in surgical patients.SENKAL:Senkal is a researcher who designed a study on enteral nutrition before and after surgical interventions.NEOPLASIA DE EST√ìMAGO:A type of stomach cancer that is often evaluated in studies related to nutritional support.NEOPLASIA DE P√ÅNCREAS:A type of pancreatic cancer that is often evaluated in studies related to nutritional support.COMPLICACIONES DE LA HERIDA:Wound complications that can occur post-surgery and are assessed in nutritional studies.NUTRICI√ìN ENTERAL INMUNOMODULADORA:Un enfoque nutricional utilizado en pacientes quir√∫rgicos para reducir infecciones y estancia hospitalariaHEPATECTOM√çAS:Un procedimiento quir√∫rgico que implica la resecci√≥n del h√≠gado, en el cual se estudi√≥ el efecto de f√≥rmulas inmunomoduladorasPACIENTES MALNUTRIDOS:Pacientes que presentan deficiencias nutricionales y que son objeto de estudio en relaci√≥n con la inmunonutrici√≥nPACIENTES BIEN NUTRIDOS:Pacientes que tienen un estado nutricional adecuado y que tambi√©n son objeto de estudio en relaci√≥n con la inmunonutrici√≥nORNITINA ALFA-CETOGLUTARATO:Un inmunonutriente que se est√° investigando por sus efectos en pacientes quemados, mostrando mejor√≠a en el balance nitrogenado.GU√çAS ASPEN:Documentos que proporcionan recomendaciones sobre el uso de f√≥rmulas inmunomoduladoras en pacientes con c√°ncer y desnutrici√≥n.GU√çAS CANADIENSES:Recomendaciones canadienses sobre el uso de f√≥rmulas nutricionales en pacientes tumorales.BURN PATIENTS:Patients who have suffered burns and are undergoing treatment, often requiring specialized nutritional supportCANCER SURGERY:Surgical procedures performed on patients with cancer, which may require immunomodulatory nutritional formulasTRIALS:Clinical trials conducted to evaluate the effectiveness of various nutritional formulas in patients with specific medical conditionsANALYSIS OF LITERATURE:A systematic review of existing literature regarding nutritional support in surgical patientsOXYGEN:A critical element for cellular metabolism, often discussed in the context of patient recovery and nutritionCENTRAL EUROPEAN JOURNAL OF IMMUNOLOGY:HUNT H:Hunt H is a researcher who co-authored studies on enteral diets after severe trauma.MOORE FA:Moore FA is a researcher who has studied the clinical benefits of immune-enhancing diets for early post-injury enteral feeding.MENDEZ C:Mendez C is a researcher who has investigated the effects of immune-enhancing diets in critically injured patients.GARCIA I:Garcia I is a researcher involved in studies on nutritional support in trauma patients.ENTERAL DIETS:Enteral diets are nutritional formulas administered through the gastrointestinal tract, often used in clinical settings for patients unable to eat normally.ANNUAL SURG:Ann Surg is a medical journal that publishes research related to surgery, including studies on enteral diets.CRITICAL CARE MED:Crit Care Med is a journal that publishes research on critical care medicine, including studies on enteral nutrition.BOWER RH:EICKHOFF U:Eickhoff U is a researcher involved in the study of perioperative enteral immunonutrition in patients undergoing elective upper gastrointestinal tract surgery.KEMEN M:Kemen M is a researcher who co-authored studies on perioperative enteral immunonutrition.PROPILS TRIAL:The PROPILS trial is a multicenter randomized controlled phase IV trial studying the interest of pre