Aº°Îº[∆èºt[∞<≤∫=¸zè<EFø<L|;∆/…º¿]ﬂ<XèºãJ©ª·å@ºèÔ<4∫ΩΩBΩıO˜<$°ªÌ™˘ªµÆŒ<[x:oÌ±;jà<›–∑:⁄*<…æª˚»ô<cóËª4≈ƒºëã;º2Éàº⁄‹Ö<¯Íaº¶dSª û"<ÍR<Ñ∆…;Qß≈<ÒE‰º&úÁºc=s:íºõ=Ë»<è≤<È„3<X›öº—!'Ω5›πaU¨º!.Èºë=1=·Ω•␀ËªFg›;t[∞<93√ºÖªºPC⁄;T”áºRY;<º¶”˚;p–;¢±º;∏Ã=ßΩÅ;u|N=XÀ<Gñª¬hΩØ2ºQúàº¨•Â;T'=…[ã:jà<'␀”ªµÆN<∫_<+ ª 9\Ω%…S<›–7<Í“º√î^ºπ˚.<`Ò¿ª_–¢º$®µπu¶;Ôµ=˚!·<å⁄Ô<µ-ª—!'<⁄ô8º@&K=lG
ΩóXº–zÓ;˝X`<]˝=pQºZ=F™*ª©BΩ@ïÛºp–<’º;ª2.;—Òº.•PªãJ©<;≠èº4<1—ª¶@:a¢∫r$±ªÖx?ºÛ;ª≤'ºŸ∞<ÿ•ÜºÛ|cº•␀hª?≠ªçÅ®ªTﬁƒº{"title": "AGENTES ANTIDIARREICOS:Medications used to treat diarrhea, including loperamide and difenoxilato."}{"title": "MEDICACIONES:Medications that may affect bowel movements and overall gastrointestinal health in patients."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROME BURIED BUMPER:El s\u00edndrome buried bumper es una complicaci\u00f3n asociada a la GEP que implica la erosi\u00f3n del freno interno de la gastrostom\u00eda a trav\u00e9s de la pared g\u00e1strica."}{"title": "F\u00cdSTULAS GASTROCOLOCUT\u00c1NEAS:Las f\u00edstulas gastrocolocut\u00e1neas son complicaciones que ocurren cuando la GEP se implanta err\u00f3neamente a trav\u00e9s del intestino grueso hasta el est\u00f3mago."}{"title": "RETIRADA PREMATURA DEL TUBO:La retirada prematura del tubo de alimentaci\u00f3n puede ocurrir si el tubo de GEP se sale debido a una holgura aumentada del orificio."}{"title": "INFECCI\u00d3N DE LA HERIDA:La infecci\u00f3n de la herida es un riesgo asociado a la realizaci\u00f3n de una intervenci\u00f3n quir\u00fargica, especialmente en pacientes con condiciones de salud comprometidas."}{"title": "DIABETES MELLITUS TIPO:La diabetes mellitus tipo es una condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica que puede aumentar el riesgo de infecci\u00f3n en pacientes que se someten a la gastrostom\u00eda endosc\u00f3pica percut\u00e1nea."}{"title": "GEP:GEP refers to Gastrostomy Enteral Feeding, a medical procedure involving the placement of a tube for nutritional support in patients who cannot eat by mouth."}{"title": "BRONCOASPIRATION:Broncoaspiration is a medical event where food or liquid enters the lungs, often leading to pneumonia and respiratory complications in patients receiving enteral nutrition."}{"title": "GRANULOMA:Granuloma formation is a complication that can occur in patients with GEP, characterized by an abnormal tissue response to irritation or infection."}{"title": "ASPIRATION PNEUMONIA:"}{"title": "DIARREA INFECCIOSA:La diarrea infecciosa es una complicaci\u00f3n que puede ocurrir en pacientes que reciben nutrici\u00f3n enteral, caracterizada por la presencia de heces l\u00edquidas causadas por infecciones."}{"title": "ESTOMA:El estoma es una abertura creada quir\u00fargicamente que permite la salida de desechos del cuerpo, y puede estar sujeto a infecciones en pacientes con nutrici\u00f3n enteral."}{"title": "HIPOFOFATEMIA:Hipofosfatemia is a condition of low phosphate levels that can occur in patients with inadequate nutritional intake or refeeding syndrome."}{"title": "AGITACI\u00d3N PSICOMOTRIZ:A condition characterized by restlessness and inability to remain still, which can occur in patients with decreased consciousness due to medical interventions"}{"title": "TRASTORNO DEPRESIVO:"}{"title": "SCCM:Society of Critical Care Medicine, which provides guidelines for nutrition support therapy in critically ill patients"}{"title": "PARROTT F:Parrott F is one of the authors involved in the multicentre trial comparing nutritional support methods in critically ill patients."}{"title": "HARRISON DA:Harrison DA is one of the authors involved in the multicentre trial comparing nutritional support methods in critically ill patients."}{"title": "SADIQUE MZ:Sadique MZ is one of the authors involved in the multicentre trial comparing nutritional support methods in critically ill patients."}{"title": "GRIEVE RD:Grieve RD is one of the authors involved in the multicentre trial comparing nutritional support methods in critically ill patients."}{"title": "CANTER RR:Canter RR is one of the authors involved in the multicentre trial comparing nutritional support methods in critically ill patients."}{"title": "BROWN B:Brown B is one of the authors discussing enteral nutrition formula selection and its implications for practice."}{"title": "ROEHL K:Roehl K is one of the authors discussing enteral nutrition formula selection and its implications for practice."}{"title": "BETZ M:Betz M is one of the authors discussing enteral nutrition formula selection and its implications for practice."}{"title": "VANDEWOUDE MF:Vandewoude MF is one of the authors discussing fibre-supplemented tube feeding in hospitalized elderly patients."}{"title": "PARIDAENS KM:Paridaens KM is one of the authors discussing fibre-supplemented tube feeding in hospitalized elderly patients."}{"title": "SUY RA:Suy RA is one of the authors discussing fibre-supplemented tube feeding in hospitalized elderly patients."}{"title": "BOONE MA:Boone MA is one of the authors discussing fibre-supplemented tube feeding in hospitalized elderly patients."}{"title": "STROBBE H:Strobbe H is one of the authors discussing fibre-supplemented tube feeding in hospitalized elderly patients."}{"title": "ENGFER MB:Engfer MB is one of the authors involved in the systematic review and meta-analysis of fibre-containing enteral formulae."}{"title": "GREEN CJ:Green CJ is one of the authors involved in the systematic review and meta-analysis of fibre-containing enteral formulae."}{"title": "SILK DB:Silk DB is one of the authors involved in the systematic review and meta-analysis of fibre-containing enteral formulae."}{"title": "VANEK VW:Vanek VW is an author recognized for significant contributions to the field of parenteral nutrition. They have authored a position paper that explores the clinical role of alternative intravenous fat emulsions, highlighting their importance in nutritional therapy. Additionally, Vanek VW is one of the authors involved in developing guidelines for nutrition support therapy specifically tailored for critically ill patients, further emphasizing their expertise and influence in this area of healthcare."}{"title": "WARREN MM:Warren MM is one of the authors discussing guidelines for nutrition support therapy in critically ill patients."}{"title": "JOHNSON DR:Johnson DR is one of the authors discussing guidelines for nutrition support therapy in critically ill patients."}{"title": "TIENGOU LE:Tiengou LE is one of the authors discussing the choice between semi-elemental and polymeric formula for enteral nutrition in acute pancreatitis."}{"title": "GLORO R:Gloro R is one of the authors discussing the choice between semi-elemental and polymeric formula for enteral nutrition in acute pancreatitis."}{"title": "POUZOULET J:Pouzoulet J is one of the authors discussing the choice between semi-elemental and polymeric formula for enteral nutrition in acute pancreatitis."}{"title": "BOUHER K:Bouhier K is one of the authors discussing the choice between semi-elemental and polymeric formula for enteral nutrition in acute pancreatitis."}{"title": "READ MH:Read MH is one of the authors discussing the choice between semi-elemental and polymeric formula for enteral nutrition in acute pancreatitis."}{"title": "ARNAUD-BATTANDIER F:Arnaud-Battandier F is one of the authors discussing the choice between semi-elemental and polymeric formula for enteral nutrition in acute pancreatitis."}{"title": "TAYLOR AL:Taylor AL is one of the authors discussing probiotic supplementation in high-risk children."}{"title": "DUNSTAN JA:Dunstan JA is one of the authors discussing probiotic supplementation in high-risk children."}{"title": "PRESCOTT SL:Prescott SL is one of the authors discussing probiotic supplementation in high-risk children."}{"title": "DEJONG C:Dejong C is one of the authors discussing ESPEN guidelines on enteral nutrition in gastroenterology."}{"title": "HAMMARQVIST F:Hammarqvist F is one of the authors discussing ESPEN guidelines on enteral nutrition in gastroenterology."}{"title": "HEBUTERNE X:Hebuterne X is a researcher recognized for significant contributions to the field of home enteral nutrition and its practices across Europe. Additionally, Hebuterne X is one of the authors involved in discussing the European Society for Clinical Nutrition and Metabolism (ESPEN) guidelines pertaining to enteral nutrition in gastroenterology."}{"title": "MCMANON MM:McMahon MM is one of the authors discussing treatment outcomes of early enteral versus early parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "CLINICAL GUIDELINES TASK FORCE:The Clinical Guidelines Task Force is a specialized group within the American Society for Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition (ASPEN) dedicated to the development of clinical guidelines for nutrition support therapy. This task force focuses on creating evidence-based guidelines aimed at optimizing nutrition support for patients, ensuring that healthcare providers have access to the best practices in the field."}{"title": "HARVEY SE:"}{"title": "SOCIETY OF CRITICAL CARE MEDICINE:The Society of Critical Care Medicine (SCCM) is a professional organization dedicated to enhancing the care of critically ill patients. It focuses on various aspects of critical care, including the development of guidelines for nutrition support therapy. The organization aims to improve patient outcomes through research, education, and the establishment of best practices in critical care medicine."}{"title": "MUELLER CM:Mueller CM is an editor and contributor to various works on nutrition support and critical care."}{"title": "PETER JV:Peter JV is a researcher who has contributed to studies on treatment outcomes in hospitalized patients."}{"title": "WANG K:Wang K is a researcher involved in studies regarding enteral tube feeding intolerance."}{"title": "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARIO R\u00cdO HORTEGA:Hospital Universitario R\u00edo Hortega is a medical facility situated in Valladolid, Spain. It specializes in endocrinology and nutrition, providing comprehensive healthcare services in these fields."}{"title": "INSTITUTO DE ENDOCRINOLOG\u00cdA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N:"}{"title": "VALLADOLID:Valladolid is a city in Spain known for its significant contributions to the fields of endocrinology and nutrition. It is home to the Centro de Investigaci\u00f3n de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n, a research center dedicated to advancing knowledge in these areas. Additionally, the city houses the Hospital Cl\u00ednico Universitario, which plays a crucial role in clinical care and research. Valladolid has also been referenced in publications related to clinical nutrition and metabolism, highlighting its importance in the academic and medical communities."}{"title": "ALIMENTACI\u00d3N POR V\u00cdA ENTERAL:The method of providing nutrition directly into the gastrointestinal tract through a tube, which has been referenced since 1589."}{"title": "SONDAS:Sondas are medical devices specifically designed for enteral feeding, which includes various types of tubes such as nasogastric, nasoduodenal, and nasojejunal tubes. They are utilized to provide nutrition to patients who are unable to consume food orally. Additionally, Sondas can be used for feeding patients through gastrostomy or jejunostomy, offering a range of types and sizes to accommodate different patient needs. Overall, Sondas play a crucial role in the administration of enteral nutrition when oral intake is not feasible."}{"title": "SONDA NASOENT\u00c9RICA:A nasoenteric tube is a type of feeding tube that is inserted through the nose and extends into the small intestine, used for patients requiring long-term nutritional support."}{"title": "ALGORITMO PARA LA ELECCI\u00d3N DE ACCESO EN NUTRICI\u00d3N ENTERAL:An algorithm designed to guide the choice of access for enteral nutrition, considering patient conditions and risks."}{"title": "PEREIRA JL:Pereira JL is a researcher who plays a significant role in the recommendations for managing hyperglycemia in patients receiving artificial nutrition. Additionally, Pereira JL is recognized as an author referenced in the context of enteral nutrition guidelines and practices, contributing valuable insights to the field."}{"title": "LAPAROTOM\u00cdA:Laparotom\u00eda is a surgical procedure that involves making an incision into the abdominal cavity. This procedure is often utilized to access internal organs for various medical interventions. It may impact a patient's ability to tolerate enteral nutrition. The term \"laparotom\u00eda\" is the Spanish equivalent of \"laparotomy,\" and both descriptions highlight its role in surgical practices, particularly in relation to the abdominal wall."}{"title": "TRAUMATISMO CRANEOENCEF\u00c1LICO:Traumatismo craneoencef\u00e1lico, or cranioencephalic trauma, refers to injuries affecting both the brain and skull. This type of traumatic brain injury can complicate enteral feeding processes and may lead to serious complications, necessitating immediate medical attention. Additionally, it can result in conditions such as SIADH (Syndrome of Inappropriate Antidiuretic Hormone secretion), and the duration of treatment for such injuries can vary significantly. Overall, Traumatismo craneoencef\u00e1lico represents a critical medical condition that requires prompt and effective management."}{"title": "MIXEDEMA:Myxedema is a severe form of hypothyroidism that can affect a patient's metabolism and nutritional requirements."}{"title": "FIADOR:El fiador es un dispositivo que facilita la colocaci\u00f3n de la sonda, proporcionando rigidez y evitando la perforaci\u00f3n durante el procedimiento."}{"title": "HIGIENE BUCAL:La higiene bucal es un procedimiento que se debe mantener adecuadamente en los d\u00edas sucesivos tras la colocaci\u00f3n de la sonda para evitar complicaciones."}{"title": "RADIOL\u00d3GICA:La comprobaci\u00f3n radiol\u00f3gica es el m\u00e9todo m\u00e1s seguro para verificar la posici\u00f3n correcta de la sonda tras su colocaci\u00f3n."}{"title": "OBSTRUCCI\u00d3N:La obstrucci\u00f3n es una complicaci\u00f3n que puede ocurrir en el uso de sondas, afectando hasta el 9% de los casos."}{"title": "COMPROBACI\u00d3N:La comprobaci\u00f3n de la posici\u00f3n de la sonda es un paso crucial para asegurar su correcta colocaci\u00f3n y funcionamiento."}{"title": "PACIENTE CON RIESGO DE BRONCOASPIRACI\u00d3N:El paciente con riesgo de broncoaspiraci\u00f3n es aquel que no debe recibir una Sonda Nasog\u00e1strica debido a complicaciones potenciales."}{"title": "\u00cdLEO EN EL COLON:El \u00edleo en el colon es una condici\u00f3n que puede durar de 3 a 5 d\u00edas, afectando el tr\u00e1nsito intestinal."}{"title": "NEUMON\u00cdA ASPIRATIVA:NEUMON\u00cdA ASPIRATIVA is a serious complication that can arise from the use of enteral feeding tubes. This condition occurs when food or liquid inadvertently enters the lungs, leading to potential respiratory issues. In Spanish, it is described as a grave complication that can occur due to the entry of digestive contents into the respiratory tract."}{"title": "COMPROBACI\u00d3N RADIOLOGICA:La comprobaci\u00f3n radiol\u00f3gica es un procedimiento utilizado para confirmar la correcta colocaci\u00f3n de la sonda nasog\u00e1strica o nasoenteral."}{"title": "PONSKEY:PONSKEY is recognized as one of the pioneers of the endoscopic gastrostomy technique, significantly contributing to advancements in minimally invasive feeding procedures."}{"title": "GAUDEREZ:GAUDEREZ is a medical professional recognized for co-developing the endoscopic gastrostomy technique, which significantly improved patient care in nutritional support. In 1979, Gauderez was among the first physicians to practice endoscopic gastrostomy, contributing to the establishment of this technique as the preferred method for enteral nutrition."}{"title": "ALTERACI\u00d3N DEL NIVEL DE CONSCIENCIA:A medical condition where a patient experiences changes in awareness or responsiveness, which can be critical in assessing overall health."}{"title": "HERNIAS HIATAL:A condition where part of the stomach pushes through the diaphragm into the chest cavity, often leading to complications in digestion."}{"title": "OBSTRUCCI\u00d3N G\u00c1STRICA:A blockage in the stomach that prevents food from passing into the small intestine, requiring medical intervention."}{"title": "COMPLICACIONES INFECCIOSAS LOCALES:Local infectious complications that can arise from medical procedures, such as otitis and sinusitis, affecting patient recovery."}{"title": "COMPLICACIONES MEC\u00c1NICAS:Mechanical complications that can occur from the use of medical devices, such as injuries from pressure sores or local infections."}{"title": "CUIDADOS DE LA SONDA:The practices involved in maintaining and caring for feeding tubes to prevent complications and ensure patient safety."}{"title": "ACCESO INVASIVO AL TUBO DIGESTIVO:A medical procedure that involves creating an opening in the digestive tract for feeding or other interventions."}{"title": "PROCESOS FUNCIONALES:Functional disorders of the digestive system that may necessitate surgical interventions like enterostomies."}{"title": "INFECCIONES ABDOMINALES ACTIVAS:Active abdominal infections that can pose risks during surgical procedures, necessitating careful evaluation."}{"title": "ENFERMEDADES NEUROL\u00d3GICAS DEGENERATIVAS:Degenerative neurological diseases that can affect swallowing and digestion, leading to the need for nutritional support."}{"title": "T\u00c9CNICAS ENDOSC\u00d3PICAS:Minimally invasive procedures performed using an endoscope, often preferred for their lower risk and quicker recovery times.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "T\u00c9CNICA DE PONSKY-GAUDERER:La t\u00e9cnica de Ponsky-Gauderer es un m\u00e9todo espec\u00edfico para realizar una gastrostom\u00eda endosc\u00f3pica, que implica el uso de un endoscopio y anestesia t\u00f3pica para facilitar la inserci\u00f3n de la sonda."}{"title": "T\u00c9CNICA DE SACKS-VINE:La t\u00e9cnica de Sacks-Vine es un m\u00e9todo de colocaci\u00f3n de sonda de gastrostom\u00eda que se realiza bajo visi\u00f3n endosc\u00f3pica, utilizando una aguja introductora para guiar el cat\u00e9ter al est\u00f3mago."}{"title": "T\u00c9CNICA DE RUSSELL:La t\u00e9cnica de Russell es un procedimiento percut\u00e1neo para la colocaci\u00f3n de una sonda de gastrostom\u00eda, que utiliza un bal\u00f3n tipo Foley y control endosc\u00f3pico para asegurar la correcta colocaci\u00f3n de la sonda."}{"title": "YEYUNOSTOM\u00cdA ENDOSC\u00d3PICA:La yeyunostom\u00eda endosc\u00f3pica es un procedimiento que permite la inserci\u00f3n de una sonda en el yeyuno, indicado para pacientes con riesgo de aspiraci\u00f3n, manteniendo la motilidad y funci\u00f3n absortiva del intestino."}{"title": "ANESTESIA LOCAL:Anestesia local is a type of anesthesia utilized in various medical procedures, including faringostom\u00eda and gastrostom\u00eda endosc\u00f3pica. Its primary purpose is to minimize pain in the specific area being treated, allowing for the procedure to be performed with reduced risk of complications compared to general anesthesia. This localized approach enhances patient safety and comfort during interventions."}{"title": "FARINGOSTOM\u00cdA:Faringostom\u00eda is a surgical procedure for placing a feeding tube through the piriform sinus into the neck, indicated for trauma or malformations."}{"title": "MALFORMACIONES:Malformaciones are congenital anomalies that may require surgical procedures such as faringostom\u00eda for feeding."}{"title": "OSTOM\u00cdAS QUIR\u00daRGICAS:"}{"title": "YEYUNOSTOM\u00cdA QUIR\u00daRGICA:Yeyunostom\u00eda quir\u00fargica is a surgical procedure performed as a complement to gastrointestinal surgery to avoid risks associated with parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "T\u00c9CNICA DE STAMM:T\u00e9cnica de Stamm is a simple method for gastrostomy, suitable for high surgical risk cases or temporary gastrostomy."}{"title": "T\u00c9CNICA DE WITZEL:T\u00e9cnica de Witzel involves creating a seromuscular tunnel around the catheter to reduce leakage risk during yeyunostom\u00eda."}{"title": "T\u00c9CNICA DE JANEWAY:T\u00e9cnica de Janeway is a method for permanent gastrostomy using a Foley catheter within a gastric tunnel."}{"title": "OSTOM\u00cdAS RADIOLOGICAS:Ostom\u00edas radiol\u00f3gicas refer to procedures like gastrostom\u00eda radiol\u00f3gica percut\u00e1nea, which do not require anesthesia or endoscopy."}{"title": "ANESTESIA GENERAL:ANESTESIA GENERAL is a medical procedure utilized to induce unconsciousness in patients during surgical operations, including procedures such as the placement of feeding tubes. While it is essential for facilitating various surgeries, ANESTESIA GENERAL also carries inherent risks associated with surgical interventions."}{"title": "COMPLICACIONES DE LAS SONDAS DE YEYUNOSTOM\u00cdA:Complicaciones de las sondas de yeyunostom\u00eda refer to potential issues that can arise from the use of feeding tubes in the jejunum, including obstruction and infection."}{"title": "CAT\u00c9TER FINO:Cat\u00e9ter fino is a thin tube used in medical procedures, particularly in yeyunostom\u00eda, to facilitate feeding directly into the jejunum."}{"title": "TUBO DE ALIMENTACI\u00d3N:"}{"title": "HERNIA HIATAL:A condition where part of the stomach pushes through the diaphragm into the chest cavity, which can complicate certain medical procedures."}{"title": "ATROPINA:A medication used to reduce saliva and secretions during medical procedures, often administered subcutaneously."}{"title": "DILATADORES:Devices used to gradually widen an opening, often used in medical procedures to facilitate the insertion of catheters."}{"title": "CAT\u00c9TER DE GASTROSTOM\u00cdA:A tube inserted into the stomach for the purpose of providing nutritional support directly to patients."}{"title": "T\u00c9CNICA ENDOSC\u00d3PICA:A minimally invasive procedure that uses an endoscope to access the digestive tract for various medical interventions."}{"title": "SONDA POSTPIL\u00d3RICA:A type of feeding tube placed beyond the pylorus in the small intestine, used in patients at risk of aspiration."}{"title": "METHENY NA:Metheny NA is a researcher who has contributed to studies on feeding tube aspirates and their implications in medical practice."}{"title": "STEWART BJ:Stewart BJ is a researcher involved in studies related to nutrition and feeding tube placement."}{"title": "SMITH L:Smith L is a researcher who has co-authored studies on feeding tube aspirates."}{"title": "YAN H:Yan H is a researcher who has contributed to studies on feeding tube aspirates."}{"title": "DIEBOLD M:Diebold M is a researcher involved in studies on feeding tube aspirates."}{"title": "CLOUSE RE:Clouse RE is a researcher who has co-authored studies on feeding tube aspirates."}{"title": "HENDRY PJ:Hendry PJ is a researcher who has studied complications related to nasogastric feeding tubes."}{"title": "AKYUREKLI Y:Akyurekli Y is a researcher involved in studies on nasogastric feeding tubes."}{"title": "MCINTYRE R:Mcintyre R is a researcher who has contributed to studies on nasogastric feeding tubes."}{"title": "QUARRINGTON A:Quarrington A is a researcher involved in studies on nasogastric feeding tubes."}{"title": "KEON WJ:Keon WJ is a researcher who has studied bronchopleural complications of nasogastric feeding tubes."}{"title": "CISNEROS C:Cisneros C is a researcher who has studied the penetration of nasogastric tubes in cranial cavities."}{"title": "CANTALAPIEDRA JA:Cantalapiedra JA is a researcher involved in studies on nasogastric tube complications."}{"title": "MONTEJO JC:Montejo JC is a researcher who has contributed to studies on nasogastric tube complications."}{"title": "CASTILLO A:Castillo A is a researcher involved in studies on nasogastric tube complications."}{"title": "KITTINGER JW:Kittinger JW is a researcher who has studied the efficacy of metoclopramide in feeding tube placement."}{"title": "SANDLER RS:Sandler RS is a researcher involved in studies on feeding tube placement."}{"title": "HEIZER WD:Heizer WD is a researcher who has contributed to studies on feeding tube placement."}{"title": "KALLIAFAS S:Kalliafas S is a researcher who has studied the effects of erythromycin on feeding tube placement."}{"title": "CHOBAN PS:Choban PS is a researcher involved in studies on feeding tube placement."}{"title": "ZIEGLER D:Ziegler D is a researcher who has contributed to studies on feeding tube placement."}{"title": "DRAGO S:Drago S is a researcher involved in studies on feeding tube placement."}{"title": "FLANCAUM L:Flancbaum L is a researcher who has studied motility agents for feeding tube placement."}{"title": "PAZ HL:Paz HL is a researcher involved in studies on feeding tube placement."}{"title": "WEINAR M:Weinar M is a researcher who has contributed to studies on feeding tube placement."}{"title": "SHERMAN MS:Sherman MS is a researcher involved in studies on feeding tube placement."}{"title": "ANDREWS CP:Andrews CP is a researcher who has studied the diagnosis of nosocomial pneumonia."}{"title": "COALSON JJ:Coalson JJ is a researcher involved in studies on pneumonia diagnosis."}{"title": "SMITH JD:Smith JD is a researcher who has contributed to studies on pneumonia diagnosis."}{"title": "JOHANSON WG:Johanson WG is a researcher involved in studies on pneumonia diagnosis."}{"title": "DOTSON RG:Dotson RG is a researcher who has studied gastroesophageal reflux with nasogastric tubes."}{"title": "ROBINSON RG:Robinson RG is a researcher involved in studies on gastroesophageal reflux."}{"title": "PINGLETON SK:Pingleton SK is a researcher who has contributed to studies on gastroesophageal reflux."}{"title": "ELPERN EH:Elpern EH is a researcher who has studied pulmonary aspiration in hospitalized adults."}{"title": "IBA\u00d1EZ J:Iba\u00f1ez J is a researcher involved in studies on gastroesophageal reflux in intubated patients."}{"title": "PE\u00d1AFIEL A:Pe\u00f1afiel A is a researcher who has contributed to studies on gastroesophageal reflux."}{"title": "RAURICH JM:Raurich JM is a researcher involved in studies on gastroesophageal reflux."}{"title": "MARSE P:Marse P is a researcher who has studied the effects of patient positioning on gastroesophageal reflux."}{"title": "JORD\u00c1 R:Jord\u00e1 R is a researcher involved in studies on gastroesophageal reflux."}{"title": "MATA F:Mata F is a researcher who has contributed to studies on gastroesophageal reflux."}{"title": "CHERYL ANN MONTURO:Cheryl Ann Monturo is a researcher who has studied enteral access device selection."}{"title": "GUADERER MWL:Guaderer MWL is a researcher involved in studies on gastrostomy techniques."}{"title": "PONSKY JL:Ponsky JL is a researcher who has contributed to studies on gastrostomy techniques."}{"title": "IZANT RJ:Izant RJ is a researcher involved in studies on gastrostomy techniques."}{"title": "STIEGMANN G:Stiegmann G is a researcher who has studied operative versus endoscopic gastrostomy."}{"title": "COFF J:Coff J is a researcher involved in studies on gastrostomy techniques."}{"title": "VAN WAY C:Van Way C is a researcher who has contributed to studies on gastrostomy techniques."}{"title": "PERINO LL:Perino LL is a researcher involved in studies on gastrostomy techniques."}{"title": "PEARLMAN N:Pearlman N is a researcher who has studied gastrostomy techniques."}{"title": "NORTON L:Norton L is a researcher involved in studies on gastrostomy techniques."}{"title": "RUSSELL TR:Russell TR is a researcher who has studied percutaneous gastrostomy techniques."}{"title": "BROTMAN M:Brotman M is a researcher involved in studies on percutaneous gastrostomy."}{"title": "NORRIS P:Norris P is a researcher who has contributed to studies on percutaneous gastrostomy."}{"title": "BEATEN CGMY:Beaten CGMY is a researcher involved in studies on percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy."}{"title": "VISMANS FJFE:Vismans FJFE is a researcher who has studied percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy."}{"title": "VON MEYENFELDT MF:Von Meyenfeldt MF is a researcher involved in studies on percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy."}{"title": "DE GREGORIO MA<|(\"ENTITY\":PERSON"}{"title": "CELAYA S:Celaya S is a researcher who has contributed to studies on percutaneous gastrostomy techniques."}{"title": "CIVEIRA E:Civeira E is a researcher involved in studies on percutaneous gastrostomy."}{"title": "ALFONSO R:Alfonso R is a researcher who has studied percutaneous gastrostomy techniques."}{"title": "FERN\u00c1NDEZ J:Fern\u00e1ndez J is a researcher involved in studies on percutaneous gastrostomy."}{"title": "ARI\u00d1O I:Ari\u00f1o I is a researcher who has contributed to studies on percutaneous gastrostomy."}{"title": "CAVE DR:Cave DR is a researcher who has studied complications following percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy."}{"title": "ROBINSON WR:Robinson WR is a researcher involved in studies on complications of percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy."}{"title": "BROTSCHI EA:Brotschi EA is a researcher who has studied complications following percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy."}{"title": "DITESHEIM JA:Ditesheim JA is a researcher involved in studies on complications of percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy."}{"title": "RICHARDS W:Richards W is a researcher who has studied complications following percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy."}{"title": "SHARPK:Sharp K is a researcher involved in studies on complications of percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy."}{"title": "FATAL AND DISASTROUS COMPLICATIONS:A study focusing on the fatal and disastrous complications following percutaneous endoscopic gastrostomy."}{"title": "PERCUTANEOUS ENDOSCOPIC GASTROSTOMY:A minimally invasive technique for placing a feeding tube into the stomach."}{"title": "NASOGASTRIC FEEDING TUBES:A medical device used for delivering nutrition directly to the stomach through the nose.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "INSTITUTO DE INVESTIGACI\u00d3N DE ENDOCRINOLOG\u00cdA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N:The Instituto de Investigaci\u00f3n de Endocrinolog\u00eda y Nutrici\u00f3n is a research institute focused on endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "FACULTAD DE MEDICINA, UNIVERSIDAD DE VALLADOLID:The Facultad de Medicina at the Universidad de Valladolid is an educational institution that trains medical professionals."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL SUPLEMENTARIA:NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL SUPLEMENTARIA (NPS) es un enfoque terap\u00e9utico indicado para pacientes postquir\u00fargicos que necesitan un aporte nutricional adicional cuando la alimentaci\u00f3n enteral resulta insuficiente. Este tipo de nutrici\u00f3n complementa la alimentaci\u00f3n enteral en aquellos pacientes que no pueden satisfacer completamente sus necesidades nutricionales a trav\u00e9s de esta v\u00eda."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL HOSPITALARIA:NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL HOSPITALARIA refers to the administration of nutrients intravenously in a hospital setting. This method, known as hospital parenteral nutrition (NPH), is utilized to provide essential nutrition to patients who are unable to receive adequate nourishment through oral or enteral means. NPH is often evaluated in cost-effectiveness studies, highlighting its importance in clinical nutrition management during hospitalization."}{"title": "ENTERITIS R\u00c1DICA:La enteritis r\u00e1dica es una inflamaci\u00f3n del intestino delgado que puede resultar de la radioterapia y puede llevar a la malabsorci\u00f3n, requiriendo nutrici\u00f3n parenteral en algunos casos."}{"title": "ENTEROCOLITIS NECROTIZANTE:La enterocolitis necrotizante es una enfermedad grave que afecta principalmente a reci\u00e9n nacidos y puede causar da\u00f1o intestinal severo, a menudo requiriendo nutrici\u00f3n parenteral."}{"title": "MALFORMACIONES CONG\u00c9NITAS:Las malformaciones cong\u00e9nitas son defectos presentes al nacer que pueden afectar la estructura y funci\u00f3n del intestino, a veces requiriendo nutrici\u00f3n parenteral para el manejo nutricional."}{"title": "S\u00cdNDROMES ADHERENCIALES:Los s\u00edndromes adherenciales son condiciones en las que el tejido cicatricial causa adherencias en el intestino, lo que puede llevar a obstrucci\u00f3n y la necesidad de nutrici\u00f3n parenteral."}{"title": "ENFERMEDADES POR INCLUSI\u00d3N DE LAS MICROVELLOSIDADES:Estas enfermedades afectan la superficie intestinal y pueden causar malabsorci\u00f3n, llevando a la necesidad de nutrici\u00f3n parenteral en algunos pacientes."}{"title": "ENTERITIS AUTOINMUNES:Las enteritis autoinmunes son condiciones en las que el sistema inmunol\u00f3gico ataca el intestino, lo que puede resultar en malabsorci\u00f3n y requerir nutrici\u00f3n parenteral.)<|COMPLETE|>"}{"title": "SERVICIOS DE FARMACIA HOSPITALARIA:Los Servicios de Farmacia Hospitalaria son unidades especializadas que tienen la responsabilidad de elaborar nutrici\u00f3n parenteral individualizada. Estas unidades se enfocan en adaptar las dietas a las necesidades espec\u00edficas de cada paciente, especialmente en el contexto de pacientes cr\u00edticos. Su labor es fundamental para garantizar que cada paciente reciba la nutrici\u00f3n adecuada seg\u00fan sus requerimientos m\u00e9dicos particulares."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL INDIVIDUALIZADA:"}{"title": "ESTR\u00c9S METAB\u00d3LICO SEVERO:El estr\u00e9s metab\u00f3lico severo es una condici\u00f3n que puede contraindicar la administraci\u00f3n de nutrici\u00f3n parenteral, ya que los pacientes en esta situaci\u00f3n tienen requerimientos nutricionales especiales."}{"title": "FORMULACI\u00d3N 2 EN 1:La formulaci\u00f3n 2 en 1 es una mezcla de glucosa y amino\u00e1cidos administrada con emulsi\u00f3n lip\u00eddica de manera independiente, utilizada en nutrici\u00f3n parenteral para evitar interacciones de f\u00e1rmacos."}{"title": "FORMULACI\u00d3N 3 EN 1:La formulaci\u00f3n 3 en 1 combina amino\u00e1cidos, glucosa y l\u00edpidos en una sola bolsa, reduciendo el riesgo de contaminaci\u00f3n y la manipulaci\u00f3n durante la administraci\u00f3n."}{"title": "AA RAMIFICADOS:Los amino\u00e1cidos ramificados son un tipo de amino\u00e1cidos que se utilizan en soluciones de nutrici\u00f3n parenteral para pacientes con condiciones cr\u00edticas, como encefalopat\u00eda hep\u00e1tica."}{"title": "ENFERMEDAD DE BASE:La enfermedad de base se refiere a la condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica subyacente que afecta las necesidades nutricionales de un paciente y su tratamiento."}{"title": "D-GLUCOSA:D-Glucose is a carbohydrate that serves as a primary energy source, playing a vital role in parenteral nutrition. It influences insulin secretion and contributes to nitrogen savings, making it essential for patients who require nutritional support. Additionally, D-Glucose is responsible for a significant portion of the osmolarity of parenteral nutrition solutions, further underscoring its importance in providing energy to patients."}{"title": "GRANDES QUEMADOS:Grandes quemados refers to patients with severe burns who have increased nutritional needs due to metabolic stress."}{"title": "PACIENTES POSTQUIR\u00daRGICOS:"}{"title": "TCL INTRALIPID:TCL Intralipid is a product derived from soybean oil, used in lipid emulsions for nutritional support, particularly in providing essential fatty acids and influencing inflammatory responses."}{"title": "CLINOLEIC:Clinoleic is a 20% lipid emulsion utilized in parenteral nutrition, specifically formulated to deliver essential fatty acids. It is composed of a blend of soybean oil and olive oil, introduced in the late 1990s. Clinoleic is notable for its high content of oleic acid and vitamin E, which contribute to its nutritional benefits. As a third-generation lipid emulsion, it is enriched with olive oil, recognized for its high antioxidant content and its resistance to lipid peroxidation, making it a valuable option in clinical settings for patients requiring parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "ALPHA-TOCOPHEROL:Alpha-tocopherol is a form of vitamin E present in Clinoleic, known for its antioxidant properties and health benefits."}{"title": "ACIDOS GRASOS W3:Omega-3 fatty acids (AGW3) are incorporated into fourth-generation emulsions like Lipoplus, associated with anti-inflammatory effects."}{"title": "ACIDOS GRASOS W6:Omega-6 fatty acids (AGW6) are essential fatty acids that are present in high amounts in traditional lipid emulsions, influencing inflammatory responses."}{"title": "HIDRATACION:Hydration is a critical aspect of patient care, involving the management of fluid intake and losses to maintain health."}{"title": "BALANCE HIDRICO:Fluid balance refers to the careful management of fluid intake and output in patients to ensure proper hydration and physiological function."}{"title": "ACIDOS GRASOS:Fatty acids are key components of lipid emulsions, influencing their nutritional properties and effects on health."}{"title": "ACETATO:Acetato is a compound utilized in medical treatments, particularly recognized for its role as an additive in parenteral nutrition solutions. It serves multiple functions, including helping to maintain the body's acid-base balance and acting as a precursor to bicarbonate in cases of metabolic acidosis. Additionally, Acetato is a source of energy and is considered an essential electrolyte in the nutritional requirements for pediatric patients, particularly in parenteral nutrition. Overall, Acetato plays a crucial role in supporting the metabolic needs and pH balance of individuals receiving specialized nutritional care."}{"title": "G\u00c1STRICA:G\u00e1strica refers to the gastric secretion in the stomach, which contains specific concentrations of electrolytes."}{"title": "I. DELGADO:I. delgado refers to the small intestine, which secretes fluids containing electrolytes during digestion."}{"title": "BILIS:Bilis is a digestive fluid produced by the liver that contains electrolytes and aids in digestion."}{"title": "PACIENTE ESTABLE:A stable patient who may require less intensive monitoring and nutritional support through parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "CR\u00d3MO:Chromium is also viewed as a contaminant in parenteral nutrition and should be limited in prolonged regimens."}{"title": "GLUCEMIA CAPILAR:Capillary blood glucose monitoring is essential for patients on parenteral nutrition to ensure stable glucose levels."}{"title": "PARAMETROS CL\u00cdNICOS:Clinical parameters are essential metrics for assessing the health of patients on parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "PARAMETROS ANAL\u00cdTICOS:Analytical parameters are critical for evaluating the biochemical status of patients receiving parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "SELECION DE OLIGOELEMENTOS:"}{"title": "ASPARTATO AMINOTRANSFERASA:Aspartato Aminotransferasa is an enzyme that is commonly evaluated in blood tests to monitor liver function."}{"title": "GAMMA GLUTAMIL TRANSFERASA:Gamma Glutamil Transferasa is an enzyme that is used as a marker for liver disease and bile duct problems."}{"title": "PRUEBAS DE FUNCI\u00d3N HEP\u00c1TICA:Pruebas de Funci\u00f3n Hep\u00e1tica are a series of blood tests used to evaluate the health of the liver."}{"title": "ALANINA AMINOTRANSFERASA:"}{"title": "ALTERACIONES HEPATOBILIARES:Alteraciones hepatobiliares refer to liver and biliary tract complications that can arise from prolonged parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "C\u00c1TEDRA:C\u00e1tedra refers to the complications associated with catheter use in patients receiving parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "COMPLICACIONES DE LA NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL:"}{"title": "HIPERFOSFOREMIA:Hyperphosphatemia is a condition characterized by high phosphate levels in the blood, which can occur in patients with renal insufficiency."}{"title": "HEPATOBILIARY COMPLICATIONS:Complications that arise in the liver and bile ducts, often related to prolonged parenteral nutrition, including steatosis and cholestasis."}{"title": "INTESTINAL FAILURE:Intestinal failure is a medical condition characterized by the inability of the intestines to absorb sufficient nutrients and fluids, which often necessitates the use of parenteral nutrition. This condition predominantly affects pediatric patients, who may require home parenteral nutrition to manage their nutritional needs. Intestinal failure is considered a serious health issue and is frequently discussed in relation to liver disease and transplantation, highlighting its complexity and the critical care required for affected individuals."}{"title": "SOBRECRESCIMIENTO BACTERIANO:SOBRECRESCIMIENTO BACTERIANO is a condition characterized by an abnormal increase in bacteria in the intestines. This condition is particularly relevant for patients with intestinal failure, as it can significantly impact their liver health. In cases where patients are receiving parenteral nutrition, SOBRECRESCIMIENTO BACTERIANO may necessitate empirical treatment with metronidazole to manage the bacterial overgrowth effectively."}{"title": "TRASPLANTE AISLADO DE INTESTINO DELGADO:A surgical procedure to replace the small intestine, which can improve liver function in patients with hepatobiliary complications related to parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "HIPOMOTILIDAD INTESTINAL:La hipomotilidad intestinal es una condici\u00f3n que se refiere a la disminuci\u00f3n de la motilidad del intestino, lo que puede contribuir al fallo intestinal y a complicaciones como el sobrecrecimiento bacteriano."}{"title": "COLANGIO:El colangio es un t\u00e9rmino que se refiere a los conductos biliares, que pueden verse afectados por el flujo biliar y la salud hep\u00e1tica."}{"title": "ESTEATOSIS:La esteatosis es una acumulaci\u00f3n de grasa en el h\u00edgado que puede ser causada por la nutrici\u00f3n parenteral y otros factores, afectando la funci\u00f3n hep\u00e1tica."}{"title": "COLECISTOQUININA:La colecistoquinina es una hormona que estimula el flujo biliar y se ve afectada por la ingesta de nutrientes."}{"title": "SECRETINA:La secretina es una hormona que regula la producci\u00f3n de jugos digestivos y el flujo biliar, y su producci\u00f3n puede verse alterada en ausencia de est\u00edmulo enteral."}{"title": "MOTILINA:La motilina es una hormona que regula la motilidad gastrointestinal y puede verse afectada por la nutrici\u00f3n parenteral."}{"title": "POLIPEPTIDO PANCREATICO:El polip\u00e9ptido pancre\u00e1tico es una hormona que regula la funci\u00f3n del p\u00e1ncreas y puede influir en la digesti\u00f3n y el flujo biliar."}{"title": "OLIVEIRA FUSTER G.:Oliveira Fuster G. is an author recognized for his contributions to the field of clinical nutrition, particularly in the area of parenteral nutrition. He authored a practical guide that addresses the prescription and monitoring of parenteral nutrition, providing valuable insights for healthcare professionals. Additionally, he contributed to the \"Manual de Nutrici\u00f3n Cl\u00ednica y Diet\u00e9tica,\" further emphasizing his expertise and focus on parenteral nutrition within clinical dietary practices."}{"title": "GONZ\u00c1LEZ MOLERO I.:Gonz\u00e1lez Molero I. is a notable author and co-author in the field of clinical nutrition, particularly focusing on parenteral nutrition. They contributed to the development of a practical guide on the prescription and monitoring of parenteral nutrition, showcasing their expertise in this area. Additionally, Gonz\u00e1lez Molero I. collaborated on the \"Manual de Nutrici\u00f3n Cl\u00ednica y Diet\u00e9tica,\" further emphasizing their specialization and commitment to advancing knowledge in clinical nutrition and dietary practices."}{"title": "TRASPLANTE DE INTESTINO DELGADO:Surgical procedure indicated for selected patients with severe intestinal failure."}{"title": "DENSITOMETR\u00cdA MINERAL \u00d3SEA:Diagnostic procedure recommended for monitoring bone health in patients receiving parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "LIN LIM S.:Lin Lim S. is an author who studied the impact of malnutrition on hospitalization costs and outcomes."}{"title": "BRAGA M.:Braga M. is an author of the ESPEN guidelines on parenteral nutrition related to surgery."}{"title": "PITTIRUTI M.:Pittiruti M. is an author who contributed to the ESPEN guidelines on central venous catheters for parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "ANDERSON D.G.:Anderson D.G. is an author who researched peripheral parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "HOHEIM D.F.:Hoheim D.F. is an author who studied clinical experiences with three-in-one admixtures for parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "BAUER P.:Bauer P. is an author who researched the combination of parenteral and enteral nutrition in critically ill patients."}{"title": "DVIR D.:Dvir D. is an author who conducted an observational study on energy balance and complications in critically ill patients."}{"title": "VILLET S.:Villet S. is an author who studied the negative impact of hypocaloric feeding on clinical outcomes in ICU patients."}{"title": "KOVACEVICH D.S.:Kovacevich D.S. is an author who contributed to the standards for specialized nutrition support for home care patients."}{"title": "MIRTALLO J.:Mirtallo J. is an author involved in the task force for safe practices in parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "MIRTALLO J.M.:"}{"title": "TASK FORCE FOR THE REVISION OF SAFE PRACTICES FOR PARENTERAL NUTRITION:The \"TASK FORCE FOR THE REVISION OF SAFE PRACTICES FOR PARENTERAL NUTRITION\" is a dedicated group that focuses on establishing and revising safe practices for parenteral nutrition. This task force plays a crucial role in contributing to guidelines and recommendations within the field of nutrition support therapy, ensuring that best practices are upheld to enhance patient safety and care."}{"title": "GERMAN SOCIETY FOR NUTRITIONAL MEDICINE:A professional organization that provides guidelines and recommendations for nutritional practices in Germany, particularly in clinical settings."}{"title": "EUROPEAN SOCIETY FOR PARENTERAL AND ENTERAL NUTRITION:A society that focuses on the promotion of safe and effective nutritional practices in Europe, including guidelines for parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "SURGICAL ICU PATIENTS:Patients in the surgical intensive care unit who may require specialized nutritional support due to their critical condition."}{"title": "ROLLINS CJ:An author who has discussed total nutrient admixtures and their stability issues in nursing practice."}{"title": "ERDMAN SH:An author involved in research on central line occlusion and its implications for parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "HARDY G:HARDY G is an author recognized for significant contributions to the formulation and stability of parenteral nutrition, particularly through the development of new lipid emulsions. In addition to this, Hardy G has also discussed essential principles for compounding parenteral nutrition admixtures, further enhancing the understanding and application of nutritional support in clinical settings."}{"title": "YARANDI SS:An author who has researched amino acid composition in parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "MUNDI MS:An author who has written about the management of parenteral nutrition in hospitalized adult patients."}{"title": "KREYMANN KG:An author who has contributed to the ESPEN guidelines on enteral nutrition in intensive care."}{"title": "MCGLAVE SA:MCGLAVE SA is an author known for providing guidelines for nutrition support therapy specifically aimed at critically ill patients. Their work focuses on establishing best practices and recommendations to enhance the nutritional care of individuals facing severe health challenges."}{"title": "SUN LC:An author who has conducted a randomized controlled study on branched-chain amino acid-enriched total parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "KUHN KS:An author who has researched the role of glutamine as an indispensable nutrient in oncology."}{"title": "GIANOTTI L:An author who has conducted a randomized multicenter trial on intravenous glutamine supplementation in major abdominal surgery."}{"title": "YEH CN:An author who has researched the role of parenteral glutamine supplementation for surgical patients perioperatively."}{"title": "LUO M:An author who has studied the metabolic effects of enteral versus parenteral alanyl-glutamine dipeptide administration."}{"title": "TAPPY L:An author who has written about carbohydrates in home parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "MILLER SJ:"}{"title": "NUTRITION ADVISORY GROUP:The Nutrition Advisory Group is a committee within the American Medical Association that focuses on nutrition-related guidelines and recommendations."}{"title": "NUTRITION SUPPORT TEAMS:Nutrition support teams are multidisciplinary groups that provide guidance and management for patients requiring nutritional support, including parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "PETRINA E.:Petrina E. is a co-author of a study on hepatopathy associated with parenteral nutrition and lipid emulsions."}{"title": "ELIZONDO J.:Elizondo J. is a co-author of a study on hepatopathy associated with parenteral nutrition and lipid emulsions."}{"title": "SEIDNER DL:Seidner DL is a co-author of a position paper discussing the clinical role of alternative intravenous fat emulsions."}{"title": "ALLEN P.:Allen P. is a co-author of a position paper discussing the clinical role of alternative intravenous fat emulsions."}{"title": "DRUML W.:Druml W. is an author who researched fat elimination in chronic hepatic failure."}{"title": "FISCHER M.:Fischer M. is a co-author of a study on fat elimination in chronic hepatic failure."}{"title": "PIDLICH J.:Pidlich J. is a co-author of a study on fat elimination in chronic hepatic failure."}{"title": "LENZ K.:Lenz K. is a co-author of a study on fat elimination in chronic hepatic failure."}{"title": "BECVAROVA I.:Becvarova I. is an author who studied peroxidative protection of parenteral admixture by D-alpha-tocopherol."}{"title": "SAKER KE.:Saker KE is a co-author of a study on peroxidative protection of parenteral admixture by D-alpha-tocopherol."}{"title": "SWECKER WS JR.:Swecker WS Jr. is a co-author of a study on peroxidative protection of parenteral admixture by D-alpha-tocopherol."}{"title": "TROY GC.:Troy GC is a co-author of a study on peroxidative protection of parenteral admixture by D-alpha-tocopherol."}{"title": "MEIJER VE.:Meijer VE is an author who researched parenteral fish oil monotherapy in managing parenteral nutrition-associated liver disease."}{"title": "GURA KM.:Gura KM is a co-author of a study on parenteral fish oil monotherapy in managing parenteral nutrition-associated liver disease."}{"title": "MEISEL JA.:Meisel JA is a co-author of a study on parenteral fish oil monotherapy in managing parenteral nutrition-associated liver disease."}{"title": "LE HD.:Le HD is a co-author of a study on parenteral fish oil monotherapy in managing parenteral nutrition-associated liver disease."}{"title": "PUDER M.:Puder M. is a co-author of a study on parenteral fish oil monotherapy in managing parenteral nutrition-associated liver disease."}{"title": "WANTEN GJ.:Wanten GJ is an author who studied immune modulation by parenteral lipid emulsions."}{"title": "CALDER PC.:Calder PC is a co-author of a study on immune modulation by parenteral lipid emulsions."}{"title": "KRAFT MD.:Kraft MD is an author who reviewed phosphorus and calcium for adult nutrition support clinicians."}{"title": "MARTINEZ MJ.:Martinez MJ is a co-author of a study on hypophosphatemia in postoperative patients on total parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "MATRINEZ MA.:Matrinez MA is a co-author of a study on hypophosphatemia in postoperative patients on total parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "MONTERO M.:Montero M. is a co-author of a study on hypophosphatemia in postoperative patients on total parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "CAMPELO E.:Campelo E. is a co-author of a study on hypophosphatemia in postoperative patients on total parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "CASTRO I.:Castro I. is a co-author of a study on hypophosphatemia in postoperative patients on total parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "INARAJA MT.:Inaraja MT is a co-author of a study on hypophosphatemia in postoperative patients on total parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "F\u00c9RNANDEZ L\u00d3PEZ A MT.:Fern\u00e1ndez L\u00f3pez A MT is a co-author of a study on refeeding syndrome."}{"title": "L\u00d3PEZ OTERO B MJ.:L\u00f3pez Otero B MJ is a co-author of a study on refeeding syndrome."}{"title": "\u00c1LVAREZ V\u00c1ZQUEZ P.:\u00c1lvarez V\u00e1zquez P is a co-author of a study on refeeding syndrome."}{"title": "ARIAS DELGADO J.:Arias Delgado J is a co-author of a study on refeeding syndrome."}{"title": "OLVEIRA G.:Olveira G is an author who studied parenteral nutrition-associated hyperglycemia in non-critically ill inpatients."}{"title": "TAPIA MJ.:Tapia MJ is a co-author of a study on parenteral nutrition-associated hyperglycemia in non-critically ill inpatients."}{"title": "OC\u00d3N J.:Oc\u00f3n J is a co-author of a study on parenteral nutrition-associated hyperglycemia in non-critically ill inpatients."}{"title": "PASQUEL FJ.:Pasquel FJ is a co-author of a study on hyperglycemia during total parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "SPIEGELMAN R.:Spiegelman R is a co-author of a study on hyperglycemia during total parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "MCCAULEY M.:McCauley M is a co-author of a study on hyperglycemia during total parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "LIN LY.:Lin LY is an author who studied hyperglycemia correlating with outcomes in patients receiving total parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "LIN HC.:Lin HC is a co-author of a study on hyperglycemia correlating with outcomes in patients receiving total parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "LEE PC.:Lee PC is a co-author of a study on hyperglycemia correlating with outcomes in patients receiving total parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "MA WY.:Ma WY is a co-author of a study on hyperglycemia correlating with outcomes in patients receiving total parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "LIN HD.:Lin HD is a co-author of a study on hyperglycemia correlating with outcomes in patients receiving total parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "ZUGASTI A.:"}{"title": "VANEK VW.:"}{"title": "AMERICAN JOURNAL OF MEDICAL SCIENCES:The American Journal of Medical Sciences is a peer-reviewed medical journal that publishes research articles in various fields of medicine."}{"title": "NUTRITION CLINICAL MANUAL:The Nutrition Clinical Manual is a reference guide for clinical nutrition and dietetics, providing guidelines and recommendations for nutritional support."}{"title": "HYPERGLYCEMIA STUDY GROUP:The Hyperglycemia Study Group is a collective focused on researching hyperglycemia in patients receiving parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "LIN HC:Lin HC is a researcher involved in studies examining hyperglycemia in patients receiving total parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "LEE PC:Lee PC is a researcher who has co-authored studies on hyperglycemia and its effects on patients receiving total parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "MA WY:Ma WY is a researcher who has contributed to the understanding of hyperglycemia in the context of total parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "LIN HD:Lin HD is a researcher who has studied the correlation between hyperglycemia and patient outcomes in total parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "GARCIA-LUNA PP:Garcia-Luna PP is a researcher who has contributed to guidelines for managing hyperglycemia in non-critically ill patients."}{"title": "JAKOBY MG:Jakoby MG is a researcher who has developed an insulin protocol for managing hyperglycemia in patients receiving parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "KRINSLEY ET AL.:Krinsley et al. are researchers who studied the association between mild hypoglycemia and increased mortality in critically ill patients."}{"title": "THOMSON P:Thomson P is a researcher who has investigated vitamin D deficiency in patients receiving home parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "DUERKSEN DR:Duerksen DR is a researcher who has contributed to studies on vitamin D deficiency in patients on parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "CAVICCHI M:Cavicchi M is a researcher who has studied the prevalence of liver disease in patients receiving home parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "GABE S:Gabe S is a researcher who has examined abnormal liver function tests in patients receiving parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "LUMAN W:Luman W is a researcher who has studied the prevalence and outcomes of liver function tests in patients on home parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "LAURO A:Lauro A is a researcher who has investigated recovery from liver dysfunction after intestinal transplantation."}{"title": "O'KEEFE SF:O'Keefe SF is a researcher who has studied bacterial overgrowth and liver complications in patients with short bowel syndrome."}{"title": "TEUBNER A:Teubner A is a researcher who has studied the nutritional support of patients with enterocutaneous fistula."}{"title": "SCHWARTZ LK:Schwartz LK is a researcher who has investigated long-term treatment options for patients with intestinal failure."}{"title": "CHUNG PHY:Chung PHY is a researcher who has clinical experience in managing pediatric patients with ultra-short bowel syndrome."}{"title": "MEIJER VE:Meijer VE is a researcher who has contributed to studies on managing short bowel syndrome and nutritional support."}{"title": "LIN LY:"}{"title": "MAR\u00cdA CONCEPCI\u00d3N TERROBA LARUMBE:Mar\u00eda Concepci\u00f3n Terroba Larumbe is a medical professional associated with the Hospital Universitario R\u00edo Hortega in Valladolid, specializing in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "CRISTINA CRESPO SOTO:Cristina Crespo Soto is a medical professional associated with the Hospital Universitario R\u00edo Hortega in Valladolid, specializing in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "LUIS CU\u00c9LLAR OLMEDO:Luis Cu\u00e9llar Olmedo is a medical professional associated with the Hospital Universitario R\u00edo Hortega in Valladolid, specializing in endocrinology and nutrition."}{"title": "NUTRICI\u00d3N PARENTERAL PARCIAL:Nutrici\u00f3n parenteral parcial (NPP) is a form of parenteral nutrition that provides part of a patient's nutritional needs."}{"title": "FISH OIL-BASED LIPID EMULSIONS:Fish oil-based lipid emulsions are used to prevent and reverse parenteral nutrition-associated liver disease, as indicated by clinical experiences."}{"title": "BOSTON EXPERIENCE:The Boston experience refers to clinical findings related to the use of fish oil-based lipid emulsions in managing liver disease associated with parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "SMALL BOWEL TRANSPLANTATION:Small bowel transplantation is a medical procedure discussed in the context of its current status in the UK and internationally."}{"title": "METABOLIC BONE DISEASE:Metabolic bone disease is a condition that has been studied in patients on home parenteral nutrition, highlighting its prevalence."}{"title": "NADYA GROUP:Grupo NADYA is a group involved in research and studies related to home parenteral nutrition in Spain."}{"title": "ENTERITIS SEVERA:La enteritis severa inducida por radiaci\u00f3n es una condici\u00f3n que puede llevar a la necesidad de nutrici\u00f3n parenteral."}{"title": "F\u00cdSTULAS GASTROINTESTINALES:Las f\u00edstulas gastrointestinales con alto d\u00e9bito son condiciones que pueden impedir la nutrici\u00f3n enteral, requiriendo nutrici\u00f3n parenteral."}{"title": "ILEO POSTOPERATORIO:El \u00edleo postoperatorio persistente es una condici\u00f3n que puede requerir nutrici\u00f3n parenteral."}{"title": "COAGULOPAT\u00cdA:La coagulopat\u00eda es una condici\u00f3n m\u00e9dica que puede influir en la elecci\u00f3n del acceso venoso para la nutrici\u00f3n parenteral."}{"title": "VENAS PERIF\u00c9RICAS:Las venas perif\u00e9ricas son los vasos sangu\u00edneos de menor calibre que pueden ser utilizados para la nutrici\u00f3n parenteral, aunque con limitaciones."}{"title": "CAT\u00c9TER CENTRAL INSERTADO DE FORMA PERIF\u00c9RICA:Un cat\u00e9ter central insertado de forma perif\u00e9rica es un tipo de acceso venoso utilizado para la nutrici\u00f3n parenteral a corto plazo."}{"title": "CAT\u00c9TER VENOSO CENTRAL TUNELIZADO:Un cat\u00e9ter venoso central tunelizado es un dispositivo utilizado para la nutrici\u00f3n parenteral a largo plazo, asociado con menor incidencia de infecci\u00f3n."}{"title": "VENAS CENTRALES:"}{"title": "SUBCUTANEOUS RESERVOIR:A subcutaneous reservoir is a device implanted under the skin to provide access to the venous system for medication delivery, often used in conjunction with catheters."}{"title": "VENOUS ACCESS:Venous access refers to the medical procedures used to gain access to the venous system for treatment purposes, such as administering medications or fluids."}{"title": "SURGICAL UNIT:A surgical unit is a specialized area in a hospital where surgical procedures are performed, often under sterile conditions."}{"title": "SCLEROSIS:Sclerosis refers to the hardening of tissue, which can affect various parts of the body and may complicate venous access procedures."}{"title": "HEMIT\u00d3RAX:Hemit\u00f3rax refers to one side of the thoracic cavity, which is relevant in the context of venous access procedures to minimize complications."}{"title": "VENOUS CATHETERIZATION:Venous catheterization is the process of inserting a catheter into a vein for medical purposes, such as medication delivery or fluid administration."}{"title": "SURGICAL PROCEDURE:A surgical procedure is a medical operation performed to treat a health issue, which may involve the placement of a catheter for venous access."}{"title": "YUGULAR EXTERNA:Yugular externa is a superficial vein used for venous access, particularly visible in elderly patients, with specific advantages and disadvantages for medical procedures."}{"title": "YUGULAR INTERNA:Yugular interna is a central vein with minimal risk of pneumothorax, often used for venous access, especially when ultrasound guidance is available."}{"title": "SUBCLAVIA:Subclavia is a central vein that provides easier maintenance of dressings and is more comfortable for patients, but has a higher risk of pneumothorax."}{"title": "FEMORAL:Femoral access is a central vein that allows rapid access with a high success rate, but can impede patient mobility and has a higher risk of iliofemoral thrombosis."}{"title": "CAT\u00c9TER CENTRAL:Central catheters are used for temporary access in patients requiring infusion for more than 15 days, with specific complications associated with their use."}{"title": "CAT\u00c9TER DE INSERCI\u00d3N CENTRAL:Central insertion catheters are used for accessing the superior vena cava and have specific indications and complications."}{"title": "ACCESO VENOSO CENTRAL:"}{"title": "CAT\u00c9TERES CENTRALES:Cat\u00e9teres centrales son dispositivos m\u00e9dicos utilizados para el acceso venoso en pacientes que requieren nutrici\u00f3n parenteral o tratamientos prolongados"}{"title": "QUIR\u00d3FANO:El quir\u00f3fano es una sala en un hospital donde se realizan procedimientos quir\u00fargicos, incluyendo la inserci\u00f3n de cat\u00e9teres centrales"}{"title": "RESERVORIOS SUBCUT\u00c1NEOS IMPLANTABLES:Dispositivos venosos totalmente implantables que permiten el acceso venoso a trav\u00e9s de un cat\u00e9ter subcut\u00e1neo"}{"title": "CAT\u00c9TERES TUNELIZADOS:CAT\u00c9TERES TUNELIZADOS are central venous catheters that traverse a subcutaneous tunnel, designed to reduce the risk of infection. This method is utilized in 46.3% of patients receiving Nutritional Parenteral Diet (NPD)."}{"title": "HIGIENE DEL PACIENTE:La higiene del paciente es un factor importante que puede influir en el riesgo de infecci\u00f3n en aquellos que tienen cat\u00e9teres venosos centrales"}{"title": "EMERGENCIA:La inserci\u00f3n de cat\u00e9teres venosos centrales en situaciones de emergencia puede aumentar el riesgo de complicaciones, incluyendo infecciones"}{"title": "EMBOLISMO GASEOSO:El embolismo gaseoso es una complicaci\u00f3n que puede ocurrir por la entrada de aire en el sistema vascular durante la inserci\u00f3n de un cat\u00e9ter."}{"title": "ANTIBI\u00d3TICO:El tratamiento antibi\u00f3tico es necesario para manejar infecciones asociadas a cat\u00e9teres, junto con la posible retirada del cat\u00e9ter."}{"title": "VALSALVA:La maniobra de Valsalva es una t\u00e9cnica utilizada para prevenir el embolismo gaseoso durante la inserci\u00f3n de un cat\u00e9ter."}{"title": "TRENDENBURG:La posici\u00f3n de Trendelenburg es una t\u00e9cnica utilizada para prevenir el embolismo gaseoso durante la inserci\u00f3n de un cat\u00e9ter."}{"title": "PERSONAL EXPERIMENTADO:El personal experimentado en la inserci\u00f3n de cat\u00e9teres venosos centrales puede reducir el riesgo de complicaciones mec\u00e1nicas."}{"title": "MALPOSICI\u00d3N DEL CAT\u00c9TER:La malposici\u00f3n del cat\u00e9ter puede causar complicaciones como hemot\u00f3rax y dolor en el cuello."}{"title": "CATASTROFES MEC\u00c1NICAS:Las cat\u00e1strofes mec\u00e1nicas son complicaciones que pueden surgir durante la inserci\u00f3n de un cat\u00e9ter venoso central."}{"title": "VASCULAR ACCESS DEVICE:A vascular access device is a medical device used to deliver medications or fluids directly into the bloodstream."}{"title": "SERRETIA MARCESCENS:Serratia marcescens is a bacterium that can cause infections, particularly in patients with catheters or those who are hospitalized."}{"title": "PROTEUS MIRABILIS:Proteus mirabilis is a bacterium that can cause urinary tract infections and is associated with catheter use."}{"title": "ENTEROBACTER:"}{"title": "CAT\u00c9TER INTRAVASCULAR:An intravascular catheter is a thin, flexible tube inserted into a vein or artery to administer medication, fluids, or nutrition directly into the bloodstream."}{"title": "HIGIENE DE LAS MANOS:Hand hygiene refers to the practice of cleaning hands to prevent the spread of infections, especially in healthcare settings."}{"title": "ANTIS\u00c9PTICO:Antiseptics are substances that prevent the growth of disease-causing microorganisms, used in medical settings to clean skin and surfaces."}{"title": "POVIDONA YODADA:Povidone-iodine is an antiseptic used for skin disinfection before and after surgery, effective against a wide range of pathogens."}{"title": "UNIDADES:Units refer to specialized medical departments or facilities that provide care for patients, particularly those at high risk for infections."}{"title": "TROMBOPROFILAXIS:Thromboprophylaxis refers to the prevention of blood clots, particularly in patients with catheters, as mentioned in the guidelines."}{"title": "KUWAHARA T:Kuwahara T is a researcher who has published studies on the effects of pH and osmolality on infusion solutions for peripheral parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "ENFERMERAS ESPECIALIZADAS:"}{"title": "AMERICAN SOCIETY OF ANESTHESIOLOGISTS:The American Society of Anesthesiologists is a professional organization that provides guidelines and resources for anesthesiologists, including those related to central venous access."}{"title": "EUROPEAN JOURNAL OF RADIOLOGY:The European Journal of Radiology publishes research related to radiology, including studies on the placement of central venous catheters."}{"title": "CRITIC CARE MED:Critical Care Medicine is a journal that publishes research on critical care practices, including studies on catheter-related infections."}{"title": "W B SAUNDERS CO:W B Saunders Co is a publishing company known for producing medical literature, including textbooks and guidelines on nutrition and medical practices."}{"title": "CATHETER INFECTION:Catheter infection refers to infections that occur as a result of catheter use, which can be a significant complication in patients receiving parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "UKLEJA A:Ukleja A is an author involved in the study of patients with radiation enteritis and their treatment with home parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "KELLY DJ:Kelly DJ is an author who co-authored research on the outcomes of patients treated with home parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "DOERFLER ME:Doerfler ME is an author who researched central venous catheter placement in patients with disorders of hemostasis."}{"title": "KAUFMAN B:Kaufman B is an author who contributed to the study of central venous catheter placement in patients with hemostatic disorders."}{"title": "GOLDENBERG AS:Goldenberg AS is an author who researched central venous catheter placement in patients with disorders of hemostasis."}{"title": "POLDERMAN KH:Polderman KH is an author who studied m